s of Market Gaps for Browsers and Browser Extensions</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://essays.johnloeber.com/p/8-bundling-and-unbundling-of-email\">Bundling and Unbundling of Email</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://essays.johnloeber.com/p/7-ai-creates-returns-to-taste\">AI Creates Returns to Taste</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://essays.johnloeber.com/p/6-avoiding-polish-to-find-product\">Avoid Polish to find Product-Market-Fit</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://essays.johnloeber.com/p/5-svb-and-to-build-on-the-shoulders\">SVB and to Build on the Shoulders of Giants</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://essays.johnloeber.com/p/4-bring-back-idiomatic-design\">Bring Back Idiomatic Design</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://essays.johnloeber.com/p/3-commonalities-among-founders-in\">Commonalities among Founders in Music and Software</a></li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"yspace\">2022</div>\n        <ul>\n            <li><a href=\"https://essays.johnloeber.com/p/2-the-smartest-guys-in-the-room\">The Smartest Guys in the Room</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://essays.johnloeber.com/p/1-facebooks-intimacy-trap\">Facebook's Intimacy Trap</a></li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"yspace\">2018</div>\n        <ul>\n            <li><a href=\"https://news.crunchbase.com/venture/what-happens-to-startups-in-the-next-recession/\">What Happens to Startups in the Next Recession?</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/docs/twitter-likes.html\">Adventures in Deleting Tweets</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/fragmentation.html\">Fragmentation in Cryptocurrencies</a></li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"yspace\">2017</div>\n        <ul>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/implicit-currencies.html\">Implicit Currencies: Commerce Without Dollars</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/apple-choice.html\">Apple and Consumer Choice</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/rockefeller.html\">Notes on John D. Rockefeller</a></li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"yspace\">2016</div>\n        <ul>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/docs/kmeans.html\">K-Means Clustering on Handwritten Digits</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/twocultures.html\">Two Cultures in 2016</a></li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"yspace\">2015</div>\n        <ul>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/optimizing.html\">Optimizing for the Wrong Variable</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/docs/fama.html\">Fama-French Factors and Parameter Optimization</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/sharingeconomy.html\">Sharing Economy: Big Shifts, Big Problems</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/docs/set.html\">Set and the Elm Language</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/hackerschool.html\">Reflections on the Recurse Center</a></li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"yspace\">2014</div>\n        <ul>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/w/uber.html\">Uber, Lyft, Who Cares?</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://johnloeber.com/old_website/Honors_Combinatorics.pdf\">Honors Combinatorics Lecture Notes</a></li>\n        </ul>\n\n    ",
    "Bookshelf": "\n        <summary style=\"cursor:pointer;margin-bottom:1rem;\">\n            <span class=\"subheader\">\n               Bookshelf\n            </span>\n        </summary>\n        <p>\n            The true test of any media is\n            how much you think about it afterwards. Some thoughts take a long time to gestate.\n            Below are some of my all-time favorites: these are still often on my mind,\n            even many years later.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n        Fiction\n        </p>\n        <ul>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infinite_Jest\">Infinite Jest</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pale_King\">The Pale King</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Passenger_(McCarthy_novel)\">The Passenger</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Trial\">The Trial</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steppenwolf_(novel)\">Der Steppenwolf</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Great_Gatsby\">The Great Gatsby</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watchmen\">Watchmen</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Lear\">King Lear</a></li>\n        </ul>\n        <p>\n            Non-fiction\n        </p>\n        <ul>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.themessymiddle.com/\">The Messy Middle</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Engines-That-Markets-Alisdair-Nairn/dp/0857195999\">Engines that Move Markets</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eichmann_in_Jerusalem\">Eichmann in Jerusalem</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man%27s_Search_for_Meaning\">Man's Search for Meaning</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consider_the_Lobster\">Consider the Lobster</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    ",
    "Founding": "\n        <summary style=\"cursor:pointer;margin-bottom:1rem;\">\n            <span class=\"subheader\">\n               Founding\n            </span>\n        </summary>\n        <p>\n            My professional life is almost entirely constituted by creative partnerships with my friends.\n            I am fortunate to have helped start these companies.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n            In April 2020, I co-founded <a href=\"https://limit.com/\">Limit</a> with Alex Becker, Yoav Shaked, and Shea McNamara.\n            We changed the daily lives of thousands of insurance professionals with our two products:\n            Limit AI, a suite of AI workflow tools, and Limit Wholesale, our digital insurance brokerage.\n            I served as CEO for five years, from day one until passing the torch when we were acquired by McGowan, one of the oldest, largest,\n            and most respected insurance organizations in the United States.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n            In August 2025, Aashay Sanghvi, Patrick Mandia, and I began scoping out a new company\n            to improve personal health by focusing on environmental factors. We then co-founded <a href=\"https://rosehome.com/\">Rose</a> with\n            Eli Bronner and Henry Ellis, and have been supporting them on their journey ever since.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n            In October 2025, I co-founded <a href=\"https://green.com/\">Green</a> with Bijan Tehrani, Edward Craven, and Yoav Shaked.\n            We are building a global financial institution for the people and agents of the future.\n        </p>\n    ",
