        "All aliens defeated",
        "Alien quest complete",
        "Raptor quest: escaped",
        "Raptor quest: carrying",
        "Raptor quest: completed",
        "Aboard the Pequod",
        "Kraken defeated, aboard",
        "Kraken reward collected",
        "Guild applicant",
        "Guild member",
        "Illuminati initiate",
        "Motorcycle rented",
        "AI lab employee",
        "iPhone owned, put away",
        "iPhone equipped",
        "Robotaxi owned",
        "Software pitch pending",
        "Carrying a conservation letter",
        "Conservation letter delivered",
        "Founder funding claimed",
        "All shop hats owned",
        "Airship rented by another player",
        "Airship prepaid",
        "Airship reserved by another player",
        "Dog surfing: judging",
        "Equipment and rentals available"
      ],
      "placements": ["actor:monkey-zookeeper"],
      "shared": true
    }
  },
  "shared": {
    "ambient_001_the_miracle_in_seat_28b": {
      "id": "ambient_001_the_miracle_in_seat_28b",
      "title": "The miracle in seat 28B",
      "source_files": ["1664288374897668096.txt"],
      "tags": ["travel", "gratitude", "technology"],
      "npc_voice": "Delighted, then mildly aggrieved",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I flew across the country yesterday and complained about the pretzels. Imagine explaining that sentence to someone arriving here by covered wagon. What would impress them first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Crossing the country in an afternoon.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "They would complain about the pretzels too.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly! Then I'd ruin it by explaining boarding groups. What modern inconvenience would you defend in front of our wagon friend?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "The security line.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Nothing. Let them enjoy the miracle.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. 'Before entering the flying machine, please prove your belt is innocent.' A strange ritual, with a purpose.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "You're right. One uninterrupted afternoon of wonder. I'll keep my pretzel correspondence private.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Perhaps complaining is our oldest travel technology. What will people complain about on the first moon vacation?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "The crater view costs extra.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "The return flight was too short.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Naturally. They put you on the dark side and call it a quiet room.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Finally, an optimist! I'll save you a window seat, assuming we still have windows.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Safe travels. May your next miracle include adequate legroom.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_002_the_sandwich_championship": {
      "id": "ambient_002_the_sandwich_championship",
      "title": "The sandwich championship",
      "source_files": ["1820718320003215453.txt"],
      "tags": ["food", "ratings", "competition"],
      "npc_voice": "Earnest about a ridiculous ranking system",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Every restaurant near me has four-point-something stars. Apparently everything is excellent, except lunch. Help me settle this: should two sandwich shops have to compete head-to-head?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Absolutely. Let the sandwiches fight.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "People want different sandwiches.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A proper bracket! A tiny championship belt for the winner. First judging category?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Taste. Obviously.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Whether I can afford a second sandwich.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. Last time somebody awarded points for exposed brick. The brick was deliciously authentic, but difficult to chew.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A strong test of repeat business. I'll add a division for sandwiches that leave you financially capable of dinner.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. A spicy sandwich and a delicate cucumber sandwich should probably avoid the same weight class. How do we make the comparison fair?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Compare similar places.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Let everyone keep a personal ranking.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Same price, similar food, two recent visits. Look at us, accidentally designing a useful app over lunch.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Beautiful. I can be champion of my own extremely small sandwich jurisdiction.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy lunch. Please report any promising underdogs.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_003_the_subscription_strainer_collection": {
      "id": "ambient_003_the_subscription_strainer_collection",
      "title": "The subscription strainer collection",
      "source_files": ["1921458462489297353.txt"],
      "tags": ["shopping", "subscriptions", "habits"],
      "npc_voice": "A recent convert to reading receipts",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I went online for one strainer and bought a pack of three to justify my free-shipping membership. I now strain things at a professional level. What would you cancel first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The membership.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Nothing. Convenience is worth money.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I finally checked what I actually use. Turns out I subscribed to a memory of a good deal. What should replace my shopping habit?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Walk to a shop.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Make a list and wait a day.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I might meet a person! Possibly one willing to sell me a single object. The future is astonishing.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A cooling-off period for colanders. Sensible. My kitchen has endured enough impulsive infrastructure investment.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It can be! My friend saves hours on household supplies. How would you tell useful convenience from inertia?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Count what I actually use.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask whether I would subscribe today.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Actual use instead of imaginary future use. My exercise equipment has requested legal representation.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Ouch. That question just walked into my finances carrying a flashlight.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "If you need a strainer, please ask. Please.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_004_a_very_secure_announcement": {
      "id": "ambient_004_a_very_secure_announcement",
      "title": "A very secure announcement",
      "source_files": ["1845956688618377369.txt"],
      "tags": ["technology", "bureaucracy", "privacy"],
      "npc_voice": "Patient enough to have become dangerous",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My bank emailed me to log into its secure message center. I found a coupon for a loan. Was the coupon in danger?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Perhaps security is worth the extra steps.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The loan coupon needed witness protection.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Sometimes. But a locked door should protect something. Which message deserves the ceremony?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A genuinely private account detail.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "An apology for the extra steps.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Agreed. Give that a careful process. The promotional confetti can arrive by ordinary mail.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I would log in for that. They could even put the apology behind a second apology.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It has a new identity and a home in another inbox. What should the notification have said?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Just say it is an advertisement.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Let me choose how messages arrive.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Clear labeling! Radical transparency from the people who name fees 'adjustments.'",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A preference that survives longer than the next redesign would be lovely.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'll let you go. No password reset required.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_005_who_got_the_fare": {
      "id": "ambient_005_who_got_the_fare",
      "title": "Who got the fare",
      "source_files": ["1848143438853832840.txt"],
      "tags": ["transport", "work", "prices"],
      "npc_voice": "Chatty and genuinely curious",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My ride cost forty-seven coins. The driver said ten reached them. I spent the trip trying to work out what the other thirty-seven were driving. Who would you ask?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The company. Show the breakdown.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Could the driver set their own price?",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'd like that. Insurance, operations, fees, the whole receipt. Which number would you look at first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What the driver takes home.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "What it costs to run the service.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Same. A smooth app can make the person doing the work strangely invisible.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. My napkin accounting probably omitted something beyond 'car' and 'very confident logo.'",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Interesting. A little more bargaining, a little less mystery. Would you prefer that?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Yes, if I saw the price up front.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "I would miss predictable booking.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An agreement between two people! It sounds almost historical.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Convenience has value. I'd just like its price to introduce itself honestly.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Hope your next ride arrives promptly and pays everybody properly.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_006_the_blue_bird_committee": {
      "id": "ambient_006_the_blue_bird_committee",
      "title": "The blue bird committee",
      "source_files": ["1922316883123937347.txt"],
      "tags": ["nature", "attention", "parks"],
      "npc_voice": "Newly enthusiastic about a tiny discovery",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I used to think birdwatching sounded dull. Then one absurdly blue bird crossed my path and I followed it for twenty minutes. Have you had a hobby sneak up on you?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "I could get into birds.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "I would rather just enjoy the walk.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent. Our club currently has one member and no idea what that bird was. How shall we identify it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Listen and watch for a while.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Give it a ridiculous temporary name.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A field method! I'll put my phone away. We can be confused at a much more peaceful pace.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Professor Blue Jacket it is. Taxonomy can catch up with us later.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Entirely fair. Do you think naming everything helps us notice it, or gets in the way?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Names help me remember.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Sometimes looking is enough.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the next walk becomes a reunion. That's a lovely way to build a neighborhood.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'll let the bird remain a small blue mystery. It has not requested our paperwork.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "If you see Professor Blue Jacket, tell them the committee was impressed.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_007_the_party_badge_problem": {
      "id": "ambient_007_the_party_badge_problem",
      "title": "The party badge problem",
      "source_files": ["1931453150411804782.txt"],
      "tags": ["social", "work", "status"],
      "npc_voice": "A little starstruck, aware of it",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "At that party I kept meeting people from the same impressive lab. By the third introduction I was nodding before they said anything. What should I ask next time?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask what they actually enjoy working on.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask everyone the same silly question.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. Something a badge can't answer. What if the answer gets very technical?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask for a small example.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Admit I do not understand.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A real conversation instead of an exchange of prestigious rectangles. I could manage that.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then we both get to relax. Perhaps an excellent researcher can survive one ordinary question.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A control group! What question cuts through a room full of impressive employers?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "What is your most useless talent?",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "What did you change your mind about?",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Perfect. Tonight's keynote is now competitive napkin folding.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Ooh. That might tell me more than the biography. I'll save it for after the snack table.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy the party. The cheese has no institutional affiliation.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_008_the_bedroom_data_center": {
      "id": "ambient_008_the_bedroom_data_center",
      "title": "The bedroom data center",
      "source_files": ["1933238215085002762.txt"],
      "tags": ["technology", "independence", "tradeoffs"],
      "npc_voice": "Smug, but prepared to laugh at it",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The big cloud services went down and my bedroom server stayed up. I enjoyed eight magnificent minutes of superiority. Then its fan kept me awake. Would you run your own?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Yes. I like controlling my tools.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "No. I would rather sleep.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "There's real satisfaction in it. What would you host first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Something small that I can repair.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "My extremely important cat pictures.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Wise. My first plan was 'everything,' which is a poor incident-response strategy.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Finally, infrastructure with a mission. We must not lose the one where the cat looks like an accountant.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Valid. Somebody still has to do the maintenance. What would persuade you?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Learning how it all works.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "A very quiet server.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's the best reason. The bragging window is short, but the education sticks around.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. The ultimate technical specification: does not sound like a hair dryer at midnight.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'll see you at the next outage. Or the hardware store.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_009_thirty_five_seconds_of_spinning": {
      "id": "ambient_009_thirty_five_seconds_of_spinning",
      "title": "Thirty-five seconds of spinning",
      "source_files": ["1937613272955650115.txt"],
      "tags": ["design", "time", "customer_service"],
      "npc_voice": "Offended on behalf of everyone's afternoon",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I waited through a thirty-five-second loading animation just to download my bill. I could have drawn the bill faster. What should happen when a website wastes your time?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The designers should have to use it.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe there is a hard technical problem.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "On a slow phone, at the end of a long day. What task would you assign them?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Find one ordinary statement.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Cancel their own subscription.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. No guided demo. Let the download button defend itself.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A challenging final exam. We might need to bring snacks and an advocate.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "There might be. I'd be less annoyed if it told me what was happening. What would help?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "A useful progress message.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Let me do something else meanwhile.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "'Finding your bill' beats a spinning wheel performing interpretive dance.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Waiting feels different when it doesn't hold your whole afternoon hostage.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "You've been much quicker than the spinner. Thank you.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_010_the_pamphlet_that_picked_a_fight": {
      "id": "ambient_010_the_pamphlet_that_picked_a_fight",
      "title": "The pamphlet that picked a fight",
      "source_files": ["1939169141057036320.txt"],
      "tags": ["ideas", "reading", "disagreement"],
      "npc_voice": "Skeptical without wanting a shouting match",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "This pamphlet says everything is broken and sounds thrilled about it. I can't tell whether it explains anything. How do you judge a wonderfully angry writer?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask them to make the argument plainly.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Sometimes anger notices a real problem.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Let the idea stand without the dramatic lighting. What would count as a good answer?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A claim I could actually check.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A fair account of the other side.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A welcome change from being told that everyone who disagrees is asleep.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That would impress me. A rival who can speak in full sentences is much harder to defeat.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Certainly. A smoke alarm can be useful even if it sings badly. What comes after the alarm?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "A workable proposal.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Better questions.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. I have room for one more idea and absolutely no room for another apocalypse-themed newsletter.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'll accept that. Being dissatisfied is a beginning, not a finished reading list.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Take care. I hope your next pamphlet has both passion and footnotes.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_011_the_suspicious_philosopher": {
      "id": "ambient_011_the_suspicious_philosopher",
      "title": "The suspicious philosopher",
      "source_files": ["1946300882678599987.txt"],
      "tags": ["books", "ai", "trust"],
      "npc_voice": "A reader with a detective streak",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I bought an introduction to philosophy. The author has published forty-seven books this month, and the cover has six fingers. Where would you start the investigation?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Find out whether the author exists.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Can a generated book still be useful?",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Their biography says 'a passionate lifelong explorer of wisdom.' I could write that about a confused pigeon. What would convince you?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Specific work and verifiable references.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Read a few pages and judge those.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. Evidence gets a chair; atmospheric adjectives can stand outside.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. A real name can write nonsense too. The prose should do some actual thinking.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It might, if someone checks it and tells you what it is. What bothers you more?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Pretending there was a human expert.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Filling search results with junk.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Same. I bought someone's understanding and received an unexplained assembly process.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Every fake shortcut makes the good books harder to find. The shelf starts charging an attention tax.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your next author have a bibliography and the standard number of hands.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_012_the_snack_time_exchange_rate": {
      "id": "ambient_012_the_snack_time_exchange_rate",
      "title": "The snack-time exchange rate",
      "source_files": ["1957249901248577969.txt"],
      "tags": ["food", "exercise", "time"],
      "npc_voice": "Amused by the body's inconvenient bookkeeping",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I can eat a snack in thirty seconds and spend ages walking around afterward. My body has a very strange exchange rate. Would you rather take a long walk or sit somewhere with a really good snack?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A walk. Preferably with scenery.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The snack. Life is short.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good choice. I enjoy movement much more when it's a destination instead of a punishment. Where are we going?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Through the park.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Somewhere with a snack at the end.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent. Trees do not display a leaderboard, and I appreciate that.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An itinerary! Exercise and pleasure have agreed to share a calendar.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I respect an honest agenda. Can I persuade you to take it outside?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Yes. A bench sounds nice.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Only if you stop doing snack mathematics.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then we've improved the day without turning lunch into a moral tribunal.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Deal. The spreadsheet is closed. Tell me whether it's crunchy.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy your afternoon. You don't owe me an exercise report.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_013_the_suspiciously_ambitious_soap": {
      "id": "ambient_013_the_suspiciously_ambitious_soap",
      "title": "The suspiciously ambitious soap",
      "source_files": ["1962273196662792415.txt"],
      "tags": ["shopping", "trust", "quality"],
      "npc_voice": "Indignant, but mostly baffled",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "This refill soap is so thin it has nearly become a beverage. Same label, different seller. How would you decide whether to trust the next bottle?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Buy from a seller I can identify.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe the formula changed.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That would help. I want to know who to ask when my soap develops a new personality. What matters most?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A clear source.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A return process that works.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A chain of responsibility shorter than a detective novel.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Agreed. A guarantee becomes more convincing when it survives contact with an actual complaint.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Possible. I'm annoyed, not a laboratory. How would you check before accusing anyone?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask the maker about the batch.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Compare it with a known bottle.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Sensible. Evidence before the furious review. I shall attempt this advanced emotional technology.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. Two bottles, one sink, and perhaps a conclusive bubble.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Stay clean. Ideally with something capable of producing foam.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_014_the_seven_ticket_mystery": {
      "id": "ambient_014_the_seven_ticket_mystery",
      "title": "The seven-ticket mystery",
      "source_files": ["1972486813727244511.txt"],
      "tags": ["city", "transport", "rules"],
      "npc_voice": "Enjoys a disagreement that can stay civil",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A driver told me the speed cameras were unfair. They'd collected seven tickets. I was trying to look sympathetic while thinking about the crosswalk. Where would you start?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "With the people trying to cross.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Street design matters too.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Same. A street should be usable without rehearsing a sprint. What would make enforcement feel fair?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Clear limits and clear signs.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A way to challenge mistakes.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. The rule should be something drivers can follow before receiving an expensive souvenir.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Absolutely. A camera can be useful without becoming infallible by decree.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good point. A road that invites racing and a sign asking nicely are having different conversations. What would you change?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Make crossings shorter and calmer.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Measure whether people are safer.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Something you can feel through the steering wheel. Better than asking paint to do all the work.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Success should mean fewer frightened crossings, not an impressive stack of fines.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "See you around. I'll be crossing with the signal, at a dignified pace.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_015_a_conversation_about_tools": {
      "id": "ambient_015_a_conversation_about_tools",
      "title": "A conversation about tools",
      "source_files": [
        "1981506336329519113.txt",
        "1992828420687114452.txt",
        "2035055266434359437.txt",
        "2061707999685558330.txt"
      ],
      "tags": ["work", "learning", "competence"],
      "npc_voice": "A tired interviewer trying to stay fair",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I've heard the same polished interview answer so often I can recite it backward. I want to know whether someone enjoys understanding their tools. What would you ask?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask about a bug they actually solved.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Trivia can reject perfectly good people.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. A story with dirt on its shoes. What follow-up would reveal real understanding?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What did they try that failed?",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask them to explain it simply.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. A genuine dead end usually tells you more than a perfect victory lap.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. If the explanation needs a fog machine, we may need another question.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's fair. Hiring is a narrow window into a whole person. What would make the window better?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Let them work through a small problem.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask what they learned recently.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "And ask questions while they do it. I'd rather see thinking than a recital.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A useful invitation. Curiosity has more than one accent, and I should remember that.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks. You've improved the interview without even applying.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_016_the_phone_with_editorial_ambitions": {
      "id": "ambient_016_the_phone_with_editorial_ambitions",
      "title": "The phone with editorial ambitions",
      "source_files": ["1986240640251011307.txt"],
      "tags": ["technology", "language", "mishaps"],
      "npc_voice": "Mock-offended by an appliance",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My phone fixes words I meant to write and leaves the obvious typos alone. It recently corrected my compliment into an insult. Should I apologize, or blame the device?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Apologize. Then blame the device.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Send a voice message.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A balanced statement: personal responsibility followed by a small prosecution. What should the apology say?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "I meant congratulations.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "My phone has become my enemy.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Clean, direct, humane. The keyboard will hate it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Accurate, but now they'll ask about your phone instead of accepting the compliment. It has stolen the conversation too.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A bold return to sound. What if the dictation mangles that as well?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Actually record my voice.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Meet them and say it in person.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Ah. The original codec. Perhaps we were too quick to discard it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "No update required, though I might still stumble over the sentence on my own.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Go forth. May your next message remain the one you wrote.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_017_the_impeccable_paper_person": {
      "id": "ambient_017_the_impeccable_paper_person",
      "title": "The impeccable paper person",
      "source_files": ["1993178673810477232.txt", "1998477740492861588.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "trust", "appearances"],
      "npc_voice": "Courteous, with an increasingly raised eyebrow",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A candidate sent a glittering résumé and a strangely convincing pile of paperwork. The career began in a fancy lab; the answers sounded like a sales pitch. What would you verify first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask what they personally built.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Do not confuse nervousness with dishonesty.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A famous employer tells me where someone sat, not what they did. How would you keep it fair?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Let them show something concrete.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask the same questions of everyone.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A working example beats a wall of logos. Even a small project can have a real author.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. Suspicion should lead to a consistent process, not a talent show for my prejudices.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you. A quiet person can be excellent at work and dreadful at interviews. What would give them room?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Let them ask clarifying questions.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Verify references without making a scene.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. Actual work contains questions. We should probably allow them in the audition.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Calm and specific. My inner detective can put the enormous hat away.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Take care. I hope your next introduction requires less detective work.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_018_the_galactic_market_opportunity": {
      "id": "ambient_018_the_galactic_market_opportunity",
      "title": "The galactic market opportunity",
      "source_files": ["1993219142393250209.txt"],
      "tags": ["startups", "ambition", "incentives"],
      "npc_voice": "Absolutely straight-faced about the absurd",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm starting a company with a target market of the entire galaxy. We have no product, but the investor presentation includes several planets. What should I put on slide two?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A customer. Any customer.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Your enormous retirement plans.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A brave constraint. Apparently Jupiter has been difficult to schedule. What should I ask our first Earth customer?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What problem do you need solved?",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Would you pay for this?",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That might require changing the pitch. Terrifying. Promising, too.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A famously dangerous question for a slide deck. I'll leave space for the answer.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "You've seen through me. The founders' lounge is currently our only profitable customer segment. What would make you trust us?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Commit to building before cashing out.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Show what the team has delivered.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Reasonable. Perhaps the spaceship should exist before I choose its private dining room.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Actual progress. Dreadful for the animations budget, excellent for the company.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Keep looking up. Please do not count the stars as confirmed customers.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_019_fame_before_revenue": {
      "id": "ambient_019_fame_before_revenue",
      "title": "Fame before revenue",
      "source_files": ["1993542360949833919.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "status", "ambition"],
      "npc_voice": "Sympathetic to dreamers, suspicious of applause",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My friend makes excellent things quietly. Another friend has a famous startup that mostly makes announcements. Guess which one gets invited to speak?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The announcement specialist.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe they both deserve a little attention.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Naturally. Still, telling a story can help people attempt something difficult. When does that become worthwhile?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "When the work catches up.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "When it helps other people try.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A promise with a delivery date. I can applaud that without needing a smoke machine.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. Courage can be contagious. I'd like the inspiration to outlive the launch party.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's generous. What would you ask each of them at dinner?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "What are you proud of making?",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "What was harder than you expected?",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. A question that welcomes a useful tool and a sincere attempt.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An excellent equalizer. Even our keynote speaker must occasionally confront a printer.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "If you make something quietly today, consider this a small round of applause.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_020_the_banker_who_answers": {
      "id": "ambient_020_the_banker_who_answers",
      "title": "The banker who answers",
      "source_files": ["1993891343501021281.txt"],
      "tags": ["design", "work", "human_connection"],
      "npc_voice": "Pleasantly surprised by an old-fashioned solution",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My old bank had a maze of online forms. My new banker just asks what I need and calls to confirm. Has software ever made something harder than asking a person?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Almost every customer-service portal.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "A good form can be faster than a person.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A portal is such an ambitious name for a locked cupboard. What would your ideal version do?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Let me describe the problem in my own words.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Get a human when the form fails.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Start with the problem I have, rather than the menu they expected me to need.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A graceful escape hatch. Civilization occasionally fits inside one button.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Absolutely. I'd like the right tool for each job. Which task should stay simple and self-service?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "The thing I do every week.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Anything with a clear confirmation.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Precisely. Save the conversation for the strange cases. Don't make my rent payment a relationship exercise.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then I know what happened and can get on with my day. A surprisingly ambitious product goal.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks for the conversation. No ticket number has been created.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_021_the_neighborhood_argument_budget": {
      "id": "ambient_021_the_neighborhood_argument_budget",
      "title": "The neighborhood argument budget",
      "source_files": ["1994567789831754175.txt"],
      "tags": ["city", "politics", "cooperation"],
      "npc_voice": "An exhausted meeting attendee",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Our neighborhood meeting spent two hours on the most divisive proposal and never reached the broken crossing light. If you had one hour of everyone's goodwill, what would you spend it on?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "One useful thing we can agree on.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The difficult issue might matter most.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A crossing light feels achievable. But how do we avoid postponing every hard question forever?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Put the hard question on a real schedule.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Make the small win build trust.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. 'Later' should have a date, not a permanent apartment in the minutes.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. It is easier to disagree after discovering the other person also wants children to cross safely.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. Sometimes the awkward subject is the important one. How would you keep the room listening?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Agree on what success would look like.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask people what they are afraid of.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "We might discover we want similar things and have been fighting over the route.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A better opening than accusing them of enjoying broken traffic lights.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Wish us luck. I've brought a watch and an unreasonable hope of finishing on time.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_022_the_office_museum": {
      "id": "ambient_022_the_office_museum",
      "title": "The office museum",
      "source_files": ["1999547741287121405.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "culture", "change"],
      "npc_voice": "Fond of the past without wanting to live there",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I found our old office's ping-pong paddles. The new office has a wall about relentless optimization. Which artifact belongs in the museum?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The paddles. A gentler era.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The wall. Nobody can optimize forever.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Maybe. Though a fun office could still be a terrible job. What perk would you actually keep?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Time to have a life outside it.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "People I enjoy working with.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A benefit too large to fit on the snack shelf. I'd take it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Hard to photograph for recruiting, much easier to appreciate at six on a difficult evening.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm considering hanging it sideways and calling it a wellness intervention. What would you measure instead?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Useful work completed.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Whether people can sustain the pace.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A refreshingly concrete hobby for a workplace.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Right. A sprint is impressive; making everyone pretend the sprint is a lifestyle gets strange.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Take a paddle if you like. Its quarterly targets are very reasonable.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_023_the_streetlight_repair_economy": {
      "id": "ambient_023_the_streetlight_repair_economy",
      "title": "The streetlight repair economy",
      "source_files": ["2004960386693693525.txt", "2052046002912395409.txt"],
      "tags": ["city", "incentives", "public_goods"],
      "npc_voice": "Concerned about the street, bored by excuses",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Our streetlight lost a small bit of metal and now needs a very large repair budget. Everyone can quote the cost; nobody can tell me when the street will be bright. What would you ask?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "How do we prevent the next repair?",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Who is responsible for the result?",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. I want the lamp to illuminate the pavement, not a permanent business opportunity. Where would you start?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Test a sturdier design.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Find out why the material keeps disappearing.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A small trial, measured honestly. Much cheaper than announcing that the problem has become traditional.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Follow the actual chain of events. Better than treating every dark street as a fresh surprise.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That question causes extraordinary shuffling of papers. What result should they report?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "How long the lights actually stay on.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "The full cost to the neighborhood.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Perfect. A number that includes the street instead of merely the invoices.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Repairs cost money; darkness costs people their evening walk. The spreadsheet should notice both.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Here's hoping the next time we meet, I can actually see your face.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_024_the_armchair_civic_warrior": {
      "id": "ambient_024_the_armchair_civic_warrior",
      "title": "The armchair civic warrior",
      "source_files": ["2005119272654438865.txt"],
      "tags": ["city", "belonging", "action"],
      "npc_voice": "Loves the city and knows their own excuses",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I told my partner I'd fight for this city. They asked whether that meant attending a meeting or posting angrily from the sofa. Brutal question. What counts as showing up?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Do one small thing in person.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Writing can matter too.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "All right. No heroic soundtrack. What should I try?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Help at a neighborhood cleanup.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Go to the meeting and listen.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A visible result and perhaps a new neighbor. My sofa will endure my absence.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A difficult first mission for someone with so many opinions. Probably a useful one.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. Sometimes a clear explanation reaches people. How would I know I'm contributing rather than just venting?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Give readers an action they can take.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Check whether I learn anything.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Something beyond 'be as annoyed as me.' I can work on that.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Ouch. An excellent standard. I'll start by asking a question I don't already know my answer to.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "See you out there. Ideally somewhere beyond my own comment section.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_025_the_retired_rebel": {
      "id": "ambient_025_the_retired_rebel",
      "title": "The retired rebel",
      "source_files": ["2005904716014948545.txt"],
      "tags": ["culture", "identity", "change"],
      "npc_voice": "Amused by their own outdated pose",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An old friend built their whole identity around breaking a rule. Then the rule changed. Now they're an ordinary customer with rebellious stationery. Where does a rebel go next?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Find something worth changing.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Enjoy winning and find a new hobby.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That would be more useful than defending the jacket. What makes a cause worth it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Who it helps.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Whether I would care without an audience.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A sturdier foundation than whether it annoys somebody at dinner.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An uncomfortable test. Several of my opinions have just gone very quiet.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A surprisingly neglected option! What hobby suits a former outlaw?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Gardening.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Being pleasantly ordinary.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent. Fight the bindweed. It never acknowledges your victories.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Radical. No manifesto, no branding, just a sandwich eaten in peace.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Take care. You're allowed to grow beyond your favorite argument.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_026_the_golden_goose_committee": {
      "id": "ambient_026_the_golden_goose_committee",
      "title": "The golden goose committee",
      "source_files": ["2006057208371634487.txt"],
      "tags": ["city", "economics", "tradeoffs"],
      "npc_voice": "A practical caretaker of an elaborate metaphor",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Imagine our town has one goose laying golden eggs. Everyone agrees it should help fund the town, then argues about feathers. What's the first rule of goose policy?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Keep the goose healthy.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Find out whether there really is only one goose.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Sensible. But the town needs roads, schools, and somewhere for the goose keeper to live. How do you settle that?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Count the long-term effects.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Make the obligations predictable.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A brilliant plan for this afternoon can be a terrible plan for next spring.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then both the town and the goose can plan. Even metaphors benefit from clear rules.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent question. A fragile town should probably grow more ways to prosper. What would you invest in?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "People learning useful skills.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Reliable basic infrastructure.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "More people able to build something worthwhile. A less dramatic story, and perhaps a better town.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A good road rarely gets the keynote speech. The geese still need it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks. I'll spare you the committee's eighty-page appendix on nesting incentives.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_027_the_lucky_crook_portfolio": {
      "id": "ambient_027_the_lucky_crook_portfolio",
      "title": "The lucky crook portfolio",
      "source_files": ["2009413400724656636.txt"],
      "tags": ["ethics", "luck", "trust"],
      "npc_voice": "Firm about fairness, gentle with the listener",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Someone at dinner praised a fictional swindler for making one spectacular investment with stolen deposits. Would you call that skill?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Luck does not make the theft clever.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "There might be skill mixed in with wrongdoing.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Right. You can win a race after borrowing everyone else's bicycle without asking. What should we judge?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "How the money was obtained.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "The whole record, including the losses.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "And whether the people supplying it ever agreed to the risk. The winning ticket doesn't erase that.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. A highlight reel can turn almost any disaster into a keynote.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Possibly. We can acknowledge an ability without handing back everyone's trust. What would rebuilding trust require?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Accountability and making people whole.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "A lot more than one good prediction.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Actual repair. Much harder than a comeback interview with flattering lighting.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Trust grows from repeated honest choices, especially when honesty is inconvenient.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your brilliant opportunities include permission from the people funding them.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_028_the_potato_reset": {
      "id": "ambient_028_the_potato_reset",
      "title": "The potato reset",
      "source_files": ["2017367664302154170.txt"],
      "tags": ["food", "status", "family"],
      "npc_voice": "Comfortably delighted by something simple",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "In the city I debate tasting menus. Visiting family, I eat potatoes with salt and think they're marvelous. Has my palate been lying to me?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The company changes the meal.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe the potatoes are just very good.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I think so. A familiar kitchen does extraordinary things to an ordinary potato. What would you bring to that table?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Something everyone remembers.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A new dish to share.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then dinner comes with a story instead of a sales description.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Lovely. Tradition can make room for a guest without losing its chair.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An agricultural explanation! What would be your test of an excellent meal?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Would I want it again tomorrow?",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Can I enjoy it without describing it?",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A strong standard. Several prestigious foams have failed it immediately.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Dinner can survive without becoming content.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy your next meal. It is allowed to be uncomplicated.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_029_the_airport_pocket_puzzle": {
      "id": "ambient_029_the_airport_pocket_puzzle",
      "title": "The airport pocket puzzle",
      "source_files": ["2017367664302154170.txt"],
      "tags": ["travel", "trust", "observation"],
      "npc_voice": "Curious rather than certain",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Airports feel unusually orderly to me. I started wondering why, and now my coffee has gone cold. What do you think makes a place feel safe?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Clear rules and consequences.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "People knowing what to expect.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Maybe. Though an airport has unusual rules and unusual people passing through. How would we check the idea?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Compare it with a similar busy place.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask the people working there.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. One terminal and a hunch are not a finished theory.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "People who see it daily might notice things a traveler misses while guarding a croissant.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's interesting. A sign can sometimes do more than a warning. What would you borrow for city life?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Directions that actually help.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Enough people around to ask.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Being lost makes every small problem feel more threatening.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A staffed place feels different from a silent system. I like that explanation, though I'll keep wondering.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Safe travels. I'll continue my research by finally drinking this coffee.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_030_the_moral_accounting_office": {
      "id": "ambient_030_the_moral_accounting_office",
      "title": "The moral accounting office",
      "source_files": ["2018247911847678378.txt"],
      "tags": ["ethics", "reputation", "judgment"],
      "npc_voice": "Uncomfortable with overly tidy scoreboards",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A neighbor paid for a lovely public garden and treated the gardeners terribly. Someone says the donation settles the matter. Can generosity cancel cruelty?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Both things should remain on the record.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The good done still matters.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That feels right. We can enjoy the garden and still expect decent behavior. Who should get heard?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "The people who were mistreated.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Everyone affected, without flattening it.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Their experience isn't a rounding error in somebody else's generosity.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A harder conversation than assigning one enormous moral score. Probably a more honest one.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Certainly. I wouldn't uproot the flowers to prove a point. But how do we avoid selling permission to behave badly?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Separate thanks from accountability.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask whether the behavior changes.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A thank-you can be sincere without becoming a pardon.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. A beautiful gesture is a beginning; how someone treats people tomorrow still counts.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I hope you find both good company and a nice garden today.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_031_a_diary_for_a_moving_world": {
      "id": "ambient_031_a_diary_for_a_moving_world",
      "title": "A diary for a moving world",
      "source_files": ["2020276679244148906.txt"],
      "tags": ["memory", "technology", "writing"],
      "npc_voice": "A little wistful, ready to begin",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I wish I'd recorded how I worked three years ago. Every little change felt normal, and now I can't reconstruct the old normal. What would you save from today?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A completely ordinary afternoon.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "What I currently believe.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes! History keeps the grand events; someone should preserve the annoying login screen. What else belongs in the record?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What people assume will never change.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "How daily work actually feels.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Wonderful. A museum of misplaced certainty. I can contribute several exhibits.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The hesitations, the shortcuts, the tea going cold. The details the big predictions always skip.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That takes courage. Would you leave room to admit you were wrong?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "That is the point.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "I would rather record questions.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the diary can become a conversation with an earlier, overconfident version of you.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A fine approach. Questions age gracefully, and they don't demand a victory parade.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Go make a small record of the day. Future you may be glad somebody noticed.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_032_more_than_the_menu": {
      "id": "ambient_032_more_than_the_menu",
      "title": "More than the menu",
      "source_files": ["2020276679244148906.txt"],
      "tags": ["culture", "travel", "curiosity"],
      "npc_voice": "Warmly impatient with shallow conversations",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I mentioned a country I'd visited and everyone asked about the food. The food was wonderful. I also met people who do things between meals. What would you ask about?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "How ordinary life works.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Food can be a doorway into culture.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. The small customs can tell you so much. Which everyday thing interests you?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "How people welcome a guest.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "What people find funny.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A lovely question. It gives you a place at the table without treating the table as the whole culture.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes! A joke can reveal a whole set of assumptions, including the ones you have just misunderstood.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Absolutely. I just want to walk through the doorway. What question comes after 'was it tasty'?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Who taught them to make it?",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "When do people eat it together?",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then we get a person, a family, maybe a history. Much more nourishing than a restaurant ranking.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. The occasion can matter as much as the ingredients.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I hope your next journey comes with good questions and good lunch.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_033_the_landfill_archaeologist": {
      "id": "ambient_033_the_landfill_archaeologist",
      "title": "The landfill archaeologist",
      "source_files": ["2020312874024071343.txt"],
      "tags": ["environment", "tradeoffs", "systems"],
      "npc_voice": "Finds fascination in unglamorous logistics",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I used to think a tidy recycling label meant the problem was solved. Now I want to follow the truck. Where would you start if you wanted less waste?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Find out what actually gets recovered.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "A well-managed landfill can have a role.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Paper, metals, plastics: different materials have different stories. What counts as success?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Useful material actually used again.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Less material needed in the first place.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A satisfying definition. The arrow on the bin should eventually point somewhere real.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Even better. Sometimes the best sorting process is not buying the third strainer.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. Keeping things contained may beat pretending they've vanished. What should happen next?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Keep track of what is there.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Do not let that become an excuse to waste.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A slightly grim library, but perhaps a useful one for future recovery.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. 'Future archaeologists will enjoy this' is a poor defense of buying disposable everything.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks for humoring my garbage questions. I promise they're carefully sorted.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_034_the_house_with_a_thousand_rooms": {
      "id": "ambient_034_the_house_with_a_thousand_rooms",
      "title": "The house with a thousand rooms",
      "source_files": ["2020975269792841866.txt"],
      "tags": ["technology", "complexity", "judgment"],
      "npc_voice": "Excited by capability, wary of clutter",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "AI helps me build software faster, so I keep adding features. My simple tool now resembles a house where every cupboard contains another staircase. What would you do?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Decide what the thing is actually for.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "More capability can justify more complexity.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A rude but useful question. How would you draw the boundary?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Pick the user's most important task.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Write down what I will not build.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then a feature earns its room by making that task easier. The decorative staircase is nervous.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A list of peaceful absences. I should frame it above the feature backlog.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I agree. A workshop needs more tools than a picnic basket. What keeps it usable?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Good structure and clear names.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Someone willing to remove things.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "So the complexity has an address instead of hiding behind every door.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The most difficult feature request: fewer features. I'll ask for it while everyone is in a good mood.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good luck with whatever you're building. May its cupboards open normally.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_035_the_money_that_arrives_later": {
      "id": "ambient_035_the_money_that_arrives_later",
      "title": "The money that arrives later",
      "source_files": ["2022881084585943524.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "time", "priorities"],
      "npc_voice": "Reflective about a younger self",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "At twenty-three, I planned my life around equity that might pay out someday. Someday keeps rescheduling. What would you ask your younger self to consider?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "What can I enjoy or learn now?",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Patience can still be worthwhile.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Some opportunities don't wait for a liquidity event. Which would you protect?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Time with people I care about.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A chance to build useful skills.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Hard to buy back later. A sensible thing to put on the calendar before the hypothetical millions.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Something you can carry with you even if the shares never leave the spreadsheet.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Certainly. I don't regret every long bet. What would make patience feel chosen rather than imposed?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Knowing the terms and the risks.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Having some options along the way.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. 'Long term' should describe an agreement, not replace one.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Room to live while waiting. Compounding should not require placing the rest of your life in storage.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your future plans leave you a pleasant present.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_036_the_patch_that_ate_the_project": {
      "id": "ambient_036_the_patch_that_ate_the_project",
      "title": "The patch that ate the project",
      "source_files": ["2024027457763110916.txt"],
      "tags": ["technology", "maintenance", "scope"],
      "npc_voice": "A builder emerging from a long afternoon",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I asked my coding assistant to simplify something. It added a helper, then a helper for that helper. At what point am I supervising a cabinet of nesting dolls?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask it to explain the structure first.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Sometimes another viewpoint helps.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Before another line appears, show me the shape of the problem. What should the explanation contain?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What each piece is responsible for.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "What can be deleted.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then I can tell whether I've got three tools or one tool wearing three hats.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The sweetest words in maintenance. I'll clear a ceremonial space for the first removed helper.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I might be stuck arguing with the same assumptions. Who would you bring in?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Someone unfamiliar with the project.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Myself, after some sleep.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A newcomer asking 'why is this here?' can be wonderfully destructive.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A cheaper consultant with a vastly improved attitude. I'll book the appointment.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks. I'm going to close the laptop before it proposes another folder.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_037_the_croissant_alibi": {
      "id": "ambient_037_the_croissant_alibi",
      "title": "The croissant alibi",
      "source_files": ["2024918834319425608.txt"],
      "tags": ["food", "work", "city"],
      "npc_voice": "Cheerfully caught in the act",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Look at this bakery queue. Doesn't anyone work anymore? Yes, I'm in the queue. Yes, it is a weekday. How shall I explain myself?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Your computer is compiling.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "You are allowed to take a break.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent. A classic. What if my manager joins the queue?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask what their computer is compiling.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Offer to bring back breakfast.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An unexpected peer review. We'll conduct it over pastry.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A practical pivot from suspicious absence to valued team member.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A dangerously humane explanation. What would make this a proper break?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Stop checking your phone.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Actually enjoy the company.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "All right. I'll give my full professional attention to the croissant.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then hello. We've apparently been promoted from two people waiting to a conversation.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your pastry justify absolutely none of your life choices. It can just be good.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_038_the_red_album_detective": {
      "id": "ambient_038_the_red_album_detective",
      "title": "The red-album detective",
      "source_files": ["2025408296463859926.txt"],
      "tags": ["music", "design", "memory"],
      "npc_voice": "An enthusiastic collector with a peculiar search request",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm looking for a song. No title, no artist, just a red cover and a summer when I thought I could dance. Useful description?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "More useful than you think.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe you are looking for the summer.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you. My music app disagrees. What clue should I chase first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "When you added it.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "The mood or a scrap of lyric.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes! A library should remember when I fell in love with something, even if I didn't file the paperwork.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'll hum quietly. If a passing dog joins in, we may have found the genre.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Oh. That is a more expensive search. Would you play the old music or find something new?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Play the old music.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Find something new.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A brief visit, then. I don't have to move back into that haircut.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. The next excellent summer deserves its own soundtrack.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "If a red album finds you, ask whether it remembers me.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_039_terms_and_conditions_the_obstacle_course": {
      "id": "ambient_039_terms_and_conditions_the_obstacle_course",
      "title": "Terms and conditions: the obstacle course",
      "source_files": ["2027640752684339498.txt"],
      "tags": ["attention", "technology", "comedy"],
      "npc_voice": "An amateur game designer with a questionable commission",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Someone asked me to turn their legal contract into a running game so they'd finally read it. Which obstacle represents an automatic renewal?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A door that keeps sending you back.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe make the contract readable first.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Perfect. To escape, the player must understand one actual sentence. What should the game reward?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Knowing what they agreed to.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Asking a question before signing.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Confetti is fine; informed consent is the real high score.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A secret level called 'Wait, what does this mean?' More people should unlock it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An astonishingly efficient redesign. No power-ups required. What would you cut?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Needlessly tangled sentences.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Anything hiding the important terms.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The boss has been defeated by a full stop. Our legal department is reviewing the animation.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good. Put the renewal date in daylight. Let the player decide without a treasure hunt.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks for playtesting. No agreement was formed by this conversation.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_040_the_faster_tool_the_fuller_calendar": {
      "id": "ambient_040_the_faster_tool_the_fuller_calendar",
      "title": "The faster tool, the fuller calendar",
      "source_files": ["2027850363932708988.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "time", "technology"],
      "npc_voice": "Excited, with a creeping suspicion",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My new tools save so much time that I have no free time left. Every impossible project has become a weekend project. Does that sound like progress?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "You need to decide where the saved time goes.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Being able to make more is exciting.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I have been letting the project list decide. What should I reserve first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "An evening with no output.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "One project I truly care about.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An unmonetized evening. I'll try not to give it a dashboard.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the tool serves a choice, instead of manufacturing fifty new obligations.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It is! I don't want to pretend otherwise. How do I enjoy the opportunity without swallowing it whole?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Finish one thing before starting five.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Keep one old hobby on the calendar.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A harsh limitation on my collection of promising beginnings. Probably healthy.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The book on my bedside table has been waiting very patiently to become interesting again.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy your next free hour. You do get to call it free.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_041_the_weather_bet_with_footnotes": {
      "id": "ambient_041_the_weather_bet_with_footnotes",
      "title": "The weather bet with footnotes",
      "source_files": ["2028151616243937368.txt"],
      "tags": ["fairness", "games", "rules"],
      "npc_voice": "A suspicious participant with a folded rule sheet",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Our club ran a rain prediction contest. After it rained, they said sideways rain doesn't count. It was rather important to mention that earlier, wasn't it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Rules need to be clear before the bet.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Some outcomes really are ambiguous.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's my complaint. What should count as a fair repair?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Refund everyone and rewrite the rules.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Use an independent agreed measure.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A disappointing afternoon, but a cleaner start than pretending the ambiguity was a feature.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. Pick the gauge before discovering whose umbrella was open.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. A game needs a plan for the weird cases. Who should get to decide them?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Someone with nothing riding on the answer.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "The players, under rules agreed in advance.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A promising start. Preferably someone who doesn't also sell the umbrellas.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then uncertainty becomes part of the agreement instead of a trapdoor beneath it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Have a fair afternoon. May all your footnotes arrive before the result.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_042_the_young_dean_argument": {
      "id": "ambient_042_the_young_dean_argument",
      "title": "The young dean argument",
      "source_files": ["2030112252242854009.txt"],
      "tags": ["institutions", "age", "judgment"],
      "npc_voice": "Enjoys history, trying not to overread it",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I read about a thirty-year-old running a famous institution long ago. I can barely keep a houseplant alive. Have we become too suspicious of young leaders?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Sometimes experience becomes a gate.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "One famous example cannot settle it.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It can. How would you give someone a real chance without making the job a stunt?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Look at what they have already handled.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Give them authority and good support.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Specific responsibility, specific results. Better than counting birthdays or admiring a headline.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A first chance goes better when the institution wants the person to succeed.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you. My historical sample size was one very interesting paragraph. What else would you want?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Compare many institutions and eras.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask whether the job has changed.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A less thrilling evening than the anecdote, but a more reliable conclusion.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. The same title can hide a completely different mountain of work.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm off to check the houseplant. It has a young and inexperienced administration.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_043_running_with_the_internal_radio": {
      "id": "ambient_043_running_with_the_internal_radio",
      "title": "Running with the internal radio",
      "source_files": ["2031393748693955009.txt"],
      "tags": ["music", "attention", "exercise"],
      "npc_voice": "Enjoying a quiet experiment",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I forgot my headphones on a long walk. For ten minutes I was furious; then I remembered I possess thoughts. What would you listen to on a quiet walk?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Whatever the city is doing.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "I like having music with me.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "There's more rhythm here than I expected. Can you pick one sound right now?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Footsteps.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "The birds.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A small percussion section. We have been carrying the instruments all day.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A better live act than my playlist, though their release schedule is unpredictable.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "So do I. The experiment needn't become a religion. When would you turn it off?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "When I want to talk to someone.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "When the music is just filling a habit.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then hello. We appear to have found a use for the pause button.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A useful distinction. I can choose the soundtrack instead of avoiding the silence.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy the rest of your walk, with whatever soundtrack suits it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_044_the_interesting_teacher": {
      "id": "ambient_044_the_interesting_teacher",
      "title": "The interesting teacher",
      "source_files": ["2035229317756809673.txt"],
      "tags": ["learning", "status", "curiosity"],
      "npc_voice": "Fondly remembering a person rather than a credential",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My most interesting teacher never published a grand theory. They just kept asking questions nobody else asked. What makes someone good to learn from?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "They make me curious.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Expertise matters too.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. I still remember leaving class wanting to find something out. How do they do that?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "They admit what they do not know.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "They connect ideas to ordinary life.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An open door instead of a polished wall. Very inviting to a student.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Suddenly the walk home becomes part of the lesson. That's a remarkable gift.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Certainly. A charming story can still be wrong. How would you combine depth with curiosity?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask for evidence and welcome questions.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Find people who keep exploring.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That sounds like a room where learning could actually happen.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An expert with a live question is much more interesting than a certificate guarding a finished answer.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I hope you meet someone who leaves you with a good question today.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_045_the_decoy_biscuit_alarm": {
      "id": "ambient_045_the_decoy_biscuit_alarm",
      "title": "The decoy biscuit alarm",
      "source_files": ["2036531640676262187.txt"],
      "tags": ["security", "trust", "experiments"],
      "npc_voice": "Pleased with an overly elaborate household experiment",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I left a biscuit tin labeled 'important emergency biscuits' to find out who raids my cupboard. It is my very small burglar alarm. What's the flaw?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A careful thief might ignore the label.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "You have now advertised the biscuits.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. A signal isn't a guarantee. What should I do if the biscuit disappears?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Check what else was disturbed.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Make sure it was not you.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. The missing biscuit starts an investigation; it doesn't finish one.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An excellent correction. I am both the security team and a known biscuit enthusiast.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. There may be a design trade-off. What would make a better harmless alarm?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Something nobody needs to take.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Just ask people not to take them.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A small indicator, a clear signal, and fewer arguments about snack ownership.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A social solution! Cheap to deploy and surprisingly effective when people care about one another.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "If you hear an alarm, remain calm. It may be me finding crumbs.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_046_the_permanent_emperor_laundromat": {
      "id": "ambient_046_the_permanent_emperor_laundromat",
      "title": "The permanent emperor laundromat",
      "source_files": ["2037254041504223272.txt"],
      "tags": ["language", "names", "comedy"],
      "npc_voice": "Finds enormous delight in small translations",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Some company names become magnificent when translated. I'm opening a laundromat and considering 'The Eternal Sovereign.' Too much?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Not nearly enough.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "People need to know you wash clothes.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent. What should the slogan be?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Your stains have met their ruler.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A thousand years of gentle cycles.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's going over the door. The crown can sit on top of the change machine.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Majestic, though our warranty department may ask for smaller lettering.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A sensible concern from my first imaginary customer. What would you call it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "The Eternal Sovereign Laundry.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Just put a giant sock on the sign.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Clarity without surrendering the throne. I like your diplomatic instincts.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The universal heraldry of laundry. No language department required.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your garments emerge worthy of a minor monarchy.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_047_the_update_dilemma": {
      "id": "ambient_047_the_update_dilemma",
      "title": "The update dilemma",
      "source_files": ["2041664990017728776.txt"],
      "tags": ["technology", "security", "tradeoffs"],
      "npc_voice": "A cautious maintainer who misses simpler worries",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My imaginary smart kettle has two notices: 'Update immediately' and 'Never trust a new update.' It still makes tea. How should I think about this?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Find out what the update actually fixes.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Does the kettle need to be online?",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. The urgency should come from a real problem, not the color of the banner. What information would help?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A clear explanation from a trusted source.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Whether the problem affects this kettle.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then I can make a decision instead of performing a ritual of clicking.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Specifics! The great enemy of generalized panic.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A beautiful first question. Maybe some devices should simply boil. What would you keep connected?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Things where the connection adds real value.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Only what I am willing to maintain.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A useful threshold. Tea has declined to submit an account-creation request.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Right. Every connected convenience arrives with a tiny ongoing job description.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy your tea. Mine has temporarily suspended its thought leadership.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_048_the_courageous_prediction_club": {
      "id": "ambient_048_the_courageous_prediction_club",
      "title": "The courageous prediction club",
      "source_files": ["2044873916548809025.txt"],
      "tags": ["ideas", "confidence", "evidence"],
      "npc_voice": "Admires boldness but enjoys a proper scorecard",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I admire people who are right before everyone else. Unfortunately, I also remember the right predictions much better than the wrong ones. How should my prediction club keep score?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Write everything down before it happens.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Courage matters even when people miss.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Dates, terms, and all the embarrassing misses. What should we do with a very vague prediction?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask what would prove it wrong.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Keep it out of the score.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then it has to stand somewhere. 'Things will get strange' has been disqualified for universal success.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A fine thought can remain a thought. It doesn't need an undeserved trophy.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I agree. A lonely argument can be worth making. What separates courage from enjoying attention?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Being willing to revise the argument.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Having reasons beyond being contrary.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. It takes a different sort of nerve to tell your admirers you were mistaken.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An argument with a foundation! Much sturdier than a personality built around saying the opposite.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "See you next time. I predict there will be snacks, with moderate confidence.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_049_the_hometown_phrasebook": {
      "id": "ambient_049_the_hometown_phrasebook",
      "title": "The hometown phrasebook",
      "source_files": ["2045044609374711833.txt"],
      "tags": ["language", "belonging", "change"],
      "npc_voice": "A homesick traveler trying to be fair",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I went back to the place I grew up and it sounded different. At first I blamed the town. Then I wondered whether I'd packed an old version of it in my head. How would you find your way back?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Talk to the people who live there now.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Keep something familiar without freezing the place.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A homecoming should include the current occupants. What would you ask them?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What do you like about living here?",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "What has changed for you?",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A good invitation. More generous than testing everyone against my childhood memories.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then I might discover I'm not the only person trying to keep up.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I like that. What sort of thing can travel with you?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "A family expression or story.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "A habit of making newcomers welcome.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Something you can share rather than demand. That feels like a living tradition.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then home becomes a way of treating people, as well as a place I remember.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks for listening. I think I'll learn a few new names before I leave again.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_050_the_full_price_of_dinner": {
      "id": "ambient_050_the_full_price_of_dinner",
      "title": "The full price of dinner",
      "source_files": ["2046071681530442156.txt"],
      "tags": ["food", "prices", "convenience"],
      "npc_voice": "Has just discovered the rest of the receipt",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Dinner cost twenty coins. Getting it to my door cost nearly twenty more. Apparently I ordered a meal and a tiny transport company. Which part was I really buying?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "An evening without going anywhere.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "You could have enjoyed the walk.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. Some evenings that's worth a lot. How would you decide before pressing order?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Look at the final total.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask what I would rather do with the time.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "All the little numbers gathered together in daylight. A powerful shopping technology.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then convenience can be a choice with a purpose, instead of a reflex with a delivery fee.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I could. The restaurant is close enough to smell smug about it. What makes the walk worth taking?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Seeing the neighborhood.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "I just do not want to pay that much.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A meal, a change of scene, perhaps a person. Several benefits missing from the checkout page.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A completely sufficient reason. Your dinner does not require a personal growth narrative.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Whatever you choose for dinner, may the total introduce itself before the bill.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_051_the_emergency_ketchup_expedition": {
      "id": "ambient_051_the_emergency_ketchup_expedition",
      "title": "The emergency ketchup expedition",
      "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt"],
      "tags": ["food", "service", "initiative"],
      "npc_voice": "Still delighted by a tiny act of effort",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I asked a waiter for ketchup. They said yes, walked straight out of the restaurant, and returned from the corner shop with packets. What rating does that deserve?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Five stars for resourcefulness.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe the restaurant should stock ketchup.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I nearly applauded. The fries were ordinary; the mission was exceptional. What would you say?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Thanks for going out of your way.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "You have earned the title of ketchup captain.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly what I should have said. Sometimes a person deserves a clear little thank-you.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A field promotion. I'll make a badge from the empty packet, once it's clean.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Also true! Heroic effort can hide a silly system. What would you fix?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Keep the supplies where people need them.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Let the staff decide what is missing.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A humble improvement. Our ketchup captain could retire with honors.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "They probably know already. Somebody should ask before buying another decorative chalkboard.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your fries meet their condiment without an expedition.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_052_the_discount_sunrise": {
      "id": "ambient_052_the_discount_sunrise",
      "title": "The discount sunrise",
      "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt"],
      "tags": ["habits", "transport", "incentives"],
      "npc_voice": "A reluctant morning person with a receipt",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "People think I became disciplined because I arrive early. Actually, my ride costs less before breakfast. Should I tell them?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Let them admire your mysterious discipline.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Tell them. Small incentives shape habits.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Tempting. What else could I claim as part of my sunrise routine?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "An intense meditation on cheap transport.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A heroic struggle with the alarm clock.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Eyes closed, wallet open. I am one with the off-peak fare.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That part is absolutely true. There are mornings when I win by a very small margin.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "They really do. What small change would improve your morning?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Put the thing I need by the door.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Make room for an enjoyable stop.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Reduce one tiny argument with tomorrow's self. I like that.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A morning worth arriving in. Perhaps that's a stronger incentive than sternness.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "See you early, perhaps. No moral superiority will be expected.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_053_the_linen_password": {
      "id": "ambient_053_the_linen_password",
      "title": "The linen password",
      "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt"],
      "tags": ["status", "social", "belonging"],
      "npc_voice": "Baffled by a social rule nobody explained",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "At a party somebody asked whether I preferred linen or canvas. I said 'whichever is clean' and apparently failed a secret examination. What would you have said?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Linen. Then ask what I just joined.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask why they care about the distinction.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The velvet rope parts. A committee nods. How do we use our new influence?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Make the next person feel welcome.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Admit we know nothing about fabric.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A marvelous misuse of insider status. The committee will be furious.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The spell breaks. At least now we can have a real conversation about laundry.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "They might genuinely love textiles! What would separate enthusiasm from gatekeeping?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Whether they enjoy explaining it.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Whether the answer changes how they treat me.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A good enthusiast hands you a doorway rather than guarding a password.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. A preference should not become a tiny immigration office for friendship.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "You may join my club. The dress code is clothes.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_054_the_appliance_obstacle_course": {
      "id": "ambient_054_the_appliance_obstacle_course",
      "title": "The appliance obstacle course",
      "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt", "2076030398094778783.txt"],
      "tags": ["design", "technology", "comedy"],
      "npc_voice": "A person defeated by two very simple machines",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Pick my enemy: a light switch that changes brightness when I touch it, or a car trunk that beeps and opens when I try to shut it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The trunk. I know what shutting means.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The switch. Darkness should be simple.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It knows three things: beep, resist, and slowly reconsider. How should we redesign it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "One obvious button, in an obvious place.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Let a manual push work normally.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A button so recognizable it doesn't require a rental-car orientation ceremony.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A graceful fallback. My hand would like to resume its previous career.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I touch it and the room enters restaurant mode. What would your ideal switch do?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Separate on-off from dimming.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Make its state obvious by touch.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Two intentions, two controls. We may have accidentally invented clarity.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Especially when the whole point of the problem is that I cannot see.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good luck with your appliances. Mine are still deliberating.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_055_the_empty_cafe_district": {
      "id": "ambient_055_the_empty_cafe_district",
      "title": "The empty cafe district",
      "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt"],
      "tags": ["city", "community", "spaces"],
      "npc_voice": "Looking for somewhere ordinary to sit",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "This neighborhood is full of people who meet for coffee, but half the storefronts are empty. If you could open one place here, what would it be?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A comfortable, unpretentious cafe.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Somewhere to do something together.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Chairs you can sit in and music you can talk over. What would you insist on?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A place for neighbors, not just meetings.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A sandwich worth eating.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then you can arrive without an agenda. That sounds like a real neighborhood amenity.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A surprisingly rare competitive advantage. We should test the sandwich before designing the logo.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I like that. People can talk more easily with something in their hands. What activity?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Slow board games.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Repairing things.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Nothing so intense you can't finish a sentence. An excellent design brief.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A place where someone can be useful and something can leave less broken. I'd visit.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "If you find somewhere with a good chair, save me a seat.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_056_the_book_that_changed_without_moving": {
      "id": "ambient_056_the_book_that_changed_without_moving",
      "title": "The book that changed without moving",
      "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt"],
      "tags": ["books", "memory", "perspective"],
      "npc_voice": "Quietly surprised by rereading",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I reread a favorite book. At sixteen I sided with the hero; now I want to apologize to three supporting characters. Has a story ever changed sides on you?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Yes. I understand different people now.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe you read it differently the first time.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's the lovely and uncomfortable part. What do you think changed?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "I have lived through more of it.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "I notice who gets ignored.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The same page, more places for it to land. A book can wait years for part of its reader.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A small character can start looking like the person holding the whole story together.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Almost certainly. Would you preserve that first reading or replace it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Keep both.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Let the new reading win.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the book becomes a meeting place for several versions of you.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. Loving a story doesn't require maintaining every opinion you had about it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy your next chapter, including the one you have already read.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_057_the_nostalgia_counter": {
      "id": "ambient_057_the_nostalgia_counter",
      "title": "The nostalgia counter",
      "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt"],
      "tags": ["memory", "shopping", "childhood"],
      "npc_voice": "Fond of an old song, suspicious of its price",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A shop wants a fortune for the toy I loved as a child. I think they're selling ten minutes of being nine again. Would you buy it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Maybe. Some memories are worth keeping.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The old feeling might not come back.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I understand. What would make it feel like a good purchase?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "I actually want the object in my life.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "I can share the story with someone.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the memory gets a home instead of a sealed investment case.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's nice. The object becomes an excuse to tell someone where you came from.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's what worries me. What would you do instead?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Make a new memory.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Enjoy remembering without buying.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A bold entry in a market dominated by limited-edition childhoods.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An excellent price. My nine-year-old self might even approve of saving for ice cream.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I hope something pleasantly familiar finds you today, without an admission fee.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_058_the_conversation_with_a_hidden_invoice": {
      "id": "ambient_058_the_conversation_with_a_hidden_invoice",
      "title": "The conversation with a hidden invoice",
      "source_files": ["2049549461391847647.txt"],
      "tags": ["friendship", "work", "honesty"],
      "npc_voice": "Disappointed, but still open to people",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Someone asked to catch up. Forty lovely minutes later, it became a sales pitch. I felt like the first half had been rented. How should I answer next time?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask about the agenda up front.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe both parts were sincere.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A request is fine; disguising it hurts. How would you phrase it kindly?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Are we catching up, or can I help with something?",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Tell me the request first, then let us chat.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Clear without turning friendship into a customs checkpoint. I'll try it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That actually sounds generous. We can handle the business and then choose the conversation.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Possible. I'd like to leave room for that. What would make the difference?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Whether they still want to talk after a no.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Whether asking was honest.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. A friendship should survive my inability to become a customer.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A straightforward request gives me the chance to say yes without feeling maneuvered.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks for talking. There is no product reveal at the end of this.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_059_the_internet_required_to_buy_internet": {
      "id": "ambient_059_the_internet_required_to_buy_internet",
      "title": "The internet required to buy internet",
      "source_files": ["2052206951220805979.txt"],
      "tags": ["travel", "design", "accessibility"],
      "npc_voice": "Has just lost a fight with a payment screen",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "To buy airplane internet, I had to verify a payment using the internet I hadn't bought yet. Can you find the exit from this little maze?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Let people pay without opening an account.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Close the laptop. You are free.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A guest checkout! What a radical application of the word guest. What else should work?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A confirmation that works in the actual setting.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A simple fallback when the clever flow fails.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Test the airplane purchase on an airplane, not on excellent office Wi-Fi.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. Convenience should degrade gently, rather than turning into an escape room.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I did consider that. What shall I do with several disconnected hours?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Read something already on the device.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Look out of the window.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Preparation wins. A book has an astonishingly modest authentication process.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An excellent service. Occasionally cloudy, but the provider does not require a billing address.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your next purchase let you reach the paying part.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_060_a_respectable_career_in_mongering": {
      "id": "ambient_060_a_respectable_career_in_mongering",
      "title": "A respectable career in mongering",
      "source_files": ["2057490142756221296.txt"],
      "tags": ["wordplay", "work", "comedy"],
      "npc_voice": "An absurdly serious career counselor",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I've decided to become a monger. The obvious departments are fear, war, and fish. Which has the best work-life balance?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Fish. Clearly fish.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "You have overlooked cheesemongering.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A practical choice. What should go on the business card?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask me about today's catch.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "No rumors. Just haddock.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Approachable, informative, only mildly damp. You're hired as head of communications.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A firm ethical position. Our reputation will be excellent until the first disputed halibut.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good heavens. The expansion opportunities. How do we distinguish ourselves?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Responsible gouda stewardship.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "A tasteful amount of drama.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A phrase that inspires confidence and makes absolutely no nutritional promises.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "'The brie is peaking.' Finally, a crisis our customers will enjoy.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you for the consultation. May your own career remain appropriately mongered.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_061_the_productivity_bonfire": {
      "id": "ambient_061_the_productivity_bonfire",
      "title": "The productivity bonfire",
      "source_files": ["2060125830806950375.txt"],
      "tags": ["technology", "work", "measurement"],
      "npc_voice": "Holding a large bill and a small finished product",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My friend ran a swarm of AI assistants all weekend. They produced sixteen plans, nine dashboards, and no working doorbell. What should count as progress?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A doorbell somebody can use.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Planning can prevent expensive mistakes.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Right. Ringing remains our core customer need. What's the next step?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Build the smallest working version.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask why the current one fails.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "One button, one noise. We'll postpone the autonomous doorbell council.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thinking before multiplying helpers. The most economical feature yet.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. I don't want to mistake visible output for value in either direction. How would you tell useful planning from spinning?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "A plan should change a decision.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Set a limit and check what improved.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. If nothing becomes clearer, perhaps the dashboard is just a very busy wallpaper.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A small budget, a real comparison, and permission to stop. Much healthier than worshipping the meter.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Hope you get something satisfying finished today. It needn't require a swarm.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_062_the_block_we_all_want_to_live_on": {
      "id": "ambient_062_the_block_we_all_want_to_live_on",
      "title": "The block we all want to live on",
      "source_files": ["2060288816133624226.txt"],
      "tags": ["housing", "city", "tradeoffs"],
      "npc_voice": "A neighbor genuinely listening to both sides",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I want more people to afford living here. I also love this block as it is. Both feelings showed up at the housing meeting. What should we talk about first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The people who cannot get a home here.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "What the current neighbors are afraid of losing.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "They belong in the conversation, even when they aren't in the room. What would you ask for?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A real plan for more homes.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A voice for future neighbors.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Something concrete enough to debate and build, rather than a promise to value affordability forever.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A neighborhood can care about the people it has not met yet.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That might uncover a solvable problem instead of a permanent fight. What concern would you take seriously?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Transport and shared spaces.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "The character and beauty of the street.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then discuss those alongside the homes. Cars, parks, and pavements don't live in separate debates.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. We can ask how a place grows well without pretending beauty belongs only to the past.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks. I'll bring questions to the meeting, along with my badly drawn building.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_063_the_elastic_five_minutes": {
      "id": "ambient_063_the_elastic_five_minutes",
      "title": "The elastic five minutes",
      "source_files": ["2063386446728462693.txt"],
      "tags": ["transport", "trust", "time"],
      "npc_voice": "An owner of both a phone and a stopwatch",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The app said five minutes. After I booked, seven minutes. Nine minutes later, the car arrived. Have we invented a new unit of time?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The promotional minute.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Traffic really is unpredictable.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. Slightly shorter than a real minute until you commit. What would you rather see?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "An honest range.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "How reliable the estimate is.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I could plan around 'eight to twelve.' It is harder to plan around optimism in a little car icon.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A prediction with a memory of its own mistakes. That would earn some trust.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. A delay can be nobody's fault. What would make the experience less frustrating?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Explain what changed.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Give me a useful alternative.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An actual update, rather than a number quietly growing legs.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then I can choose to walk or take transit instead of watching my appointment evaporate.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'll let you go. I estimate that will take between now and immediately.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_064_the_machine_with_a_first_name": {
      "id": "ambient_064_the_machine_with_a_first_name",
      "title": "The machine with a first name",
      "source_files": ["2066804703921393850.txt"],
      "tags": ["ai", "language", "trust"],
      "npc_voice": "Curious about a small linguistic habit",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My friend says their AI 'insists' on things. My calculator has never insisted on anything, though it does disappoint me. Does a human name change how you trust a machine?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Probably. A name makes it feel social.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "People have always named their tools.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Mine feels much more confident when I imagine it wearing glasses. How should I keep that in perspective?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Check important claims.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Notice when I am treating it like a person.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Confidence is part of the voice, not a certificate attached to the answer.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A useful pause. I can enjoy a friendly interface without assigning it an inner life.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. Ships, cars, stubborn printers. Is this any different?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Conversation makes the illusion stronger.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "What matters is how well it works.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A reply can feel like company in a way a nameplate can't. That deserves some thought.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then I'll judge the answer by its usefulness, not the imagined cardigan of whoever gave it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Nice talking with you. I can confirm that I am available in person.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_065_the_book_with_a_birthday": {
      "id": "ambient_065_the_book_with_a_birthday",
      "title": "The book with a birthday",
      "source_files": ["2066804703921393850.txt"],
      "tags": ["books", "provenance", "trust"],
      "npc_voice": "Protective of an ordinary old paperback",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "This battered paperback has a date, notes in the margin, and a coffee stain older than my career. I suddenly value knowing where a text came from. Would you keep it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Absolutely. The history is part of it.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Digital copies can be preserved too.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I like thinking someone else once stopped at the same paragraph. What would you want to preserve?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "The original wording.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "The notes people left.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A reference point you can return to. Changes mean more when you can see what changed.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A little conversation across time, including one reader who strongly disagreed with chapter seven.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Certainly. Paper can vanish, and a file can be carefully kept. What gives you confidence in a copy?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "A clear source and version history.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Several independent ways to check it.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then convenience and provenance can sit on the same shelf.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Trust gets stronger when you can compare, instead of merely being reassured.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your next book arrive with a good story and a knowable past.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_066_the_imperfect_good_person": {
      "id": "ambient_066_the_imperfect_good_person",
      "title": "The imperfect good person",
      "source_files": ["2066804703921393850.txt"],
      "tags": ["ethics", "habits", "kindness"],
      "npc_voice": "Sincere, with no interest in moral grandstanding",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm trying to live more kindly, and discovering I cannot turn my entire life into a perfectly consistent argument. How do you improve without becoming unbearable?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Pick one change you can sustain.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Keep questioning the contradictions.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That sounds more promising than my twelve-point personal constitution. What sort of change?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Something that reduces a harm I care about.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Treat the people around you better.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A specific commitment, made honestly. Small enough to keep doing is a real strength.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. I shouldn't become so devoted to humanity that I stop listening to the person in front of me.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I should. Comfort can become an excuse very quietly. How would you keep the questioning useful?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Be honest without demanding perfection.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Let the standard guide you, not consume you.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then a mistake can lead to repair rather than a theatrical collapse.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A direction to walk in. I can do that without putting the whole street on trial.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks for a kind conversation. That already improved part of the day.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_067_the_invisible_stadium": {
      "id": "ambient_067_the_invisible_stadium",
      "title": "The invisible stadium",
      "source_files": ["2066804703921393850.txt"],
      "tags": ["sports", "imagination", "play"],
      "npc_voice": "An enthusiastic listener to something you cannot see",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I listened to a whole match on the radio and somehow saw it. My brain supplied a stadium the size of a teacup. Want to try a little commentary?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Describe the most ordinary action dramatically.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "How do you know the picture is accurate?",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "All right: 'The stranger approaches the crossing. A glance left. A glance right. An entire afternoon rests on this decision!' Your finish?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A clean crossing! The crowd erupts!",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "They have stopped to tie a shoe.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A flawless pedestrian performance. We'll be discussing this one in the studio for hours.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A devastating tactical pause. The commentators must now discuss the player's entire childhood.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I don't. The commentator gives me enough to care, and my mind fills the rest. What detail matters most?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Where things are happening.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "What is at stake.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A little geography, and suddenly the action has somewhere to live.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A moving dot can become a story once you know what someone hopes it will do.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "And the stranger walks away. A strong finish, warmly received by the booth.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_068_the_tiny_browser_game_revival": {
      "id": "ambient_068_the_tiny_browser_game_revival",
      "title": "The tiny browser-game revival",
      "source_files": ["2066804703921393850.txt"],
      "tags": ["games", "creativity", "nostalgia"],
      "npc_voice": "An enthusiastic tinkerer",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I miss little browser games made by one person with one strange idea. You opened a page and became a penguin accountant. What tiny game would you make?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A game about running this conversation.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Something you can finish in five minutes.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent. The player earns no coins, but might leave slightly amused. What's the main obstacle?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Getting the stranger to stop talking.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Finding an unexpectedly good question.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A worthy final boss. I will try to offer a fair exit.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the whole game fits in one lovely moment. I would play it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A complete little experience! What feeling should it leave?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "I figured something out.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "I want to show a friend.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A tiny click in the mind. No enormous progress bar required.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A game with enough personality to survive the walk between two desks.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks for the design meeting. The penguin's accounts remain a serious concern.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_069_the_bigger_pile_of_quests": {
      "id": "ambient_069_the_bigger_pile_of_quests",
      "title": "The bigger pile of quests",
      "source_files": ["2066804703921393850.txt"],
      "tags": ["games", "achievement", "leisure"],
      "npc_voice": "A player defending their evening",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "One game keeps teaching me harder things. Another keeps giving me more things to collect. Both can be fun, but I feel very different afterward. What brings you back?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Getting better at something.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "A comfortable world to spend time in.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That satisfying moment when the impossible becomes ordinary. What kind of challenge works for you?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "One I can understand and practice.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A puzzle with a surprising insight.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair difficulty. I want to know what I learned, not wonder whether the game secretly changed the rules.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A good little revelation can outlast an evening of filling bars.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's real enjoyment too. Not every evening needs an exam. How do you know you're still having fun?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "I would choose it without the daily rewards.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "I can stop when I want to.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A useful test. The world itself should offer you a reason to stay.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the routine belongs to you. A nice place to visit should also let you leave.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy the world at your own pace. You don't owe every icon an appointment.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_070_the_surprisingly_possible_trip": {
      "id": "ambient_070_the_surprisingly_possible_trip",
      "title": "The surprisingly possible trip",
      "source_files": ["2067959225440186478.txt"],
      "tags": ["travel", "assumptions", "adventure"],
      "npc_voice": "Has just questioned a logistical superstition",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I assumed getting to Tahoe meant renting a car and conducting a small administrative campaign. Then I found a driver happy to take the trip. What else are we assuming is impossible?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Maybe just ask before inventing the obstacles.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "You still need a way back.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes! I had already held three imaginary negotiations and lost all of them. What would you ask first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Can you do this trip, and what will it cost?",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "What would make the arrangement work for both of us?",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Two useful questions. Far more effective than my private seminar on why nobody would agree.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. A long trip can be an opportunity for one person and a relief for another.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you. My enthusiasm was traveling one-way. What should we check?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "The return plan and timing.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "The conditions and everyone's comfort.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A mountain sunset is nicer when it isn't also a transport emergency.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Sensible. Easy to arrange doesn't mean every trip or every day is the same.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your next journey involve fewer imaginary obstacles and a definite ride home.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_071_the_ordinary_day_defense": {
      "id": "ambient_071_the_ordinary_day_defense",
      "title": "The ordinary-day defense",
      "source_files": ["2069441547301691547.txt"],
      "tags": ["friendship", "wellbeing", "attention"],
      "npc_voice": "Gentle, grounded, unhurried",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Lately I've started admiring people who remain kind, curious, and reasonably steady. It sounds modest until you watch how loud the world gets. What helps you stay grounded?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "People who can tell me when I am drifting.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Small routines in the real world.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A friend who can disagree without making it a performance is precious. How do you make that easier?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Actually listen when they speak.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Spend time together outside arguments.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Inviting honesty means leaving it somewhere safe to land.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A walk, a meal, a shared task. Reminders that a person is more than their latest opinion.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Those help me too. What would you keep even during a very busy week?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "A walk without the feed.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "A regular conversation with someone.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Give the actual street a turn to set the scale of things.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A good anchor. Some days a simple 'how are you?' carries more weight than an enormous explanation.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Take care of yourself. Ordinary good days are worth keeping.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_072_the_glamorous_employee_option": {
      "id": "ambient_072_the_glamorous_employee_option",
      "title": "The glamorous employee option",
      "source_files": ["2070412397731557657.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "ambition", "status"],
      "npc_voice": "Cheerfully suspicious of career mythology",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Everyone at dinner said they should start a company. One person quietly admitted they love their job. The room treated it like a confession. Which path sounds ambitious to you?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Doing excellent work can be ambitious.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "I would still like to make my own thing.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I think so. What would you want from a good job?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Useful responsibility and room to learn.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "People and work I believe in.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A real stretch without needing to invent an entire payroll department first.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A stronger foundation than choosing a title for how it sounds over appetizers.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then that's worth taking seriously. How would you tell desire from the glamour around it?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Would I want the actual daily work?",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Try building something small first.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An excellent question. The calendar often tells the truth the biography leaves out.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the ambition gets a pair of working shoes before it gets a dramatic portrait.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good luck with your work, whatever noun goes on the business card.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_073_the_sentence_doing_a_u_turn": {
      "id": "ambient_073_the_sentence_doing_a_u_turn",
      "title": "The sentence doing a U-turn",
      "source_files": ["2071424116977262918.txt"],
      "tags": ["writing", "ai", "language"],
      "npc_voice": "A playful editor with a pencil",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm editing a paragraph that reverses itself every sentence. By the end, I'm seasick. Want to help it walk in a straight line?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Give me the worst sentence.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "A reversal can be effective.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "'The bench is not merely seating; it is the architecture of collective possibility.' What would you write?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "It is a good place to sit together.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "The bench has two people on it.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you. The bench has returned safely to the pavement.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A fact! We can let the reader discover the collective possibility without a brass band.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Of course. I like a turn when the thought actually turns. How do we keep it from becoming a tic?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Use it where the contrast matters.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Read the whole passage aloud.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the sentence earns its dramatic entrance.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. The ear notices when every sentence wears the same little magician's cape.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'll let you go in a reasonably straight line.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_074_the_warning_and_the_window_fan": {
      "id": "ambient_074_the_warning_and_the_window_fan",
      "title": "The warning and the window fan",
      "source_files": ["2071980538102227027.txt"],
      "tags": ["climate", "planning", "city"],
      "npc_voice": "Practical, tired of purely ceremonial concern",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Our building has had years of meetings about hotter summers. We also have one elderly fan and a window that opens halfway. What should the next meeting produce?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "An actual plan to keep people cool.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The building may be hard to change.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Especially the people with the fewest options. What belongs in the first step?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Check who is most exposed and what already works.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Assign responsibility and a date.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Start with real rooms and real people. A sensible improvement over another alarming slideshow.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then concern gets a calendar. The fan would appreciate the backup.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. Old buildings don't rearrange themselves because the forecast gets worse. How do we work with that?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Compare practical options before choosing.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Budget for preparation instead of just emergencies.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Some changes can happen sooner than others. We can start somewhere without pretending the rest is solved.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Less dramatic than a rescue, much nicer for the people who would need rescuing.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Stay comfortable out there. I hope the next forecast meets a prepared room.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_075_the_little_coin_satchel": {
      "id": "ambient_075_the_little_coin_satchel",
      "title": "The little coin satchel",
      "source_files": ["2072427700044935558.txt"],
      "tags": ["money", "memory", "everyday_life"],
      "npc_voice": "Affectionately amused by changing habits",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My partner asked what to do when we have too many coins. I explained carrying a little bag to the bank as a child. Apparently I am now a traveling historical exhibit. What would you do with a jar of coins?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Count it and deposit it.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Keep some for small everyday things.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A satisfying ceremony. Did you ever have a passbook or a savings tin?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Yes. Watching it grow was exciting.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "No, that sounds ancient.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A physical trace of patience. The coins made a marvelous noise on the way there.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It was after the invention of chairs, I assure you. Barely.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I like having money you can actually hear. What should the jar be for?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "An occasional treat.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Helping when somebody is short.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then each little coin contributes to a future pleasant afternoon.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A good use for spare change. The jar can be a tiny neighborhood institution.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your pockets remain pleasantly weighted and your trousers structurally sound.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_076_the_contractor_invented_my_surname": {
      "id": "ambient_076_the_contractor_invented_my_surname",
      "title": "The contractor invented my surname",
      "source_files": ["2072898264639099278.txt"],
      "tags": ["language", "home", "mishaps"],
      "npc_voice": "Still laughing at a belated realization",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "For months my contractor called me 'Alex Parnter.' I signed deliveries that way. Today I saw their contacts: 'Alex partner of Sam.' Have I acquired a family name?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Congratulations, the Parnter dynasty begins.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "You should probably clear it up.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "We need a coat of arms. What should it feature?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A crooked door and two crossed pencils.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A phone refusing to correct the spelling.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent. Beneath them: 'Close Enough, Pending Approval.'",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Our ancestral enemy. Every generation shall inherit one slightly wrong contact card.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I know. They've been perfectly polite, and I kept assuming it meant something. How would you tell them?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Laugh and explain the mix-up.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask what they have me saved as.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. We can solve it without putting anybody on trial for a typo.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A brave question. There may be more of my biography hidden in that phone.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Take care. The Parnters send their regards.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_077_the_podcast_cafe_experiment": {
      "id": "ambient_077_the_podcast_cafe_experiment",
      "title": "The podcast cafe experiment",
      "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
      "tags": ["social", "audio", "city"],
      "npc_voice": "An enthusiastic host testing a dubious idea",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Bars show games and cafes play music. I'm considering a place where people listen to a podcast together. Welcoming idea, or a hostage situation with muffins?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "It depends on whether people chose it.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "I would rather hear the people in the room.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Agreed. No surprise three-hour interview during a quiet breakfast. What would make the event work?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A short episode and time to talk.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "A clearly announced topic.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the recording starts a conversation instead of replacing one.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. People should know whether they're entering a discussion of history or nineteen microphones arguing about protein.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. A room should not need famous distant people to become interesting. What would you host instead?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Everyone brings one good question.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Quiet time with optional conversation.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A remarkably low-cost booking strategy, and much better chances of being heard.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An event that permits both company and peace. We may have reinvented a pleasant cafe.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks for the feedback. Your muffin remains free of compulsory audio.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_078_the_hotel_with_expensive_socks": {
      "id": "ambient_078_the_hotel_with_expensive_socks",
      "title": "The hotel with expensive socks",
      "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
      "tags": ["travel", "design", "tradeoffs"],
      "npc_voice": "A practical admirer of beautiful things",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "One hotel had gorgeous lamps and charged a fortune to wash a sock. The cheaper place had a laundry room. What should a nice hotel be nice at?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Making the stay easy.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Beautiful surroundings can be worth paying for.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Sleep, clean clothes, a shower I can operate. What's your nonnegotiable?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A genuinely comfortable bed.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Controls I can understand while tired.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A shocking focus on the activity named in 'bedroom.' I support it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. I should not need to solve the lighting console to become unconscious.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "They can. I've brought home ideas from lovely rooms. How would you judge the design?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Whether it helps me feel at ease.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Whether I want to borrow an idea.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then beauty includes how the room treats you, not just how it photographs.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A little inspiration can travel home very cheaply. Far more cheaply than the laundry bill.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Sleep well wherever you stay. May your socks be treated as ordinary garments.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_079_the_washing_machine_appreciation_society": {
      "id": "ambient_079_the_washing_machine_appreciation_society",
      "title": "The washing-machine appreciation society",
      "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
      "tags": ["technology", "gratitude", "work"],
      "npc_voice": "Earnest about a very ordinary miracle",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I washed clothes by hand for a few days. I now greet the washing machine with genuine respect. What ordinary invention deserves a small ceremony?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Clean running water.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The refrigerator.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Absolutely. A quiet system doing immense work. What should the ceremony include?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Thank the people maintaining it.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Actually look after the infrastructure.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Miracles turn out to have crews and maintenance schedules.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An excellent offering. The pipes have very little use for applause.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A strong nominee. Leftovers alone could make the case. What would you miss first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Keeping food for another day.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Cold drinks when it is hot.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A little more time and a little less waste, every day. That's a powerful gift.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A modest pleasure with a long engineering story behind it. Worth a grateful sip.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your household miracles keep humming quietly.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_080_the_epic_with_a_voice": {
      "id": "ambient_080_the_epic_with_a_voice",
      "title": "The epic with a voice",
      "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
      "tags": ["books", "audio", "storytelling"],
      "npc_voice": "An excited listener to an old story",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I kept failing to read an old epic. Then I heard it aloud and suddenly wanted to know what happened next. Have I been using the wrong doorway?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Some stories want a voice.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "You can listen and still look at the words.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I think so. The rhythm started doing work I couldn't see on the page. What makes a good storyteller?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "They know where to pause.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "They make people feel present.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A silence that makes you lean forward. Hard to reproduce with a very determined bookmark.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Suddenly the distant voyage contains somebody trying to get home.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's a good idea. I could stop treating formats like rival sports teams. What would you listen for?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "The repeated patterns.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "What makes me curious.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The little landmarks that help you travel through a long story.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the point is finding the story, not winning a private test of stamina.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy your next story. You may enter through whichever doorway opens.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_081_one_draw_three_wrong_labels": {
      "id": "ambient_081_one_draw_three_wrong_labels",
      "title": "One draw, three wrong labels",
      "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt", "2103521027779420606.txt"],
      "tags": ["puzzle", "learning", "play"],
      "npc_voice": "An inviting puzzle enthusiast",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Quick puzzle? Three boxes contain apples, oranges, or a mix. Their labels say APPLES, ORANGES, and MIXED, but every label is wrong. You may draw one fruit from one box. Which box?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The one labeled MIXED.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The one labeled APPLES.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Since its label is wrong, it contains only one kind. You draw an apple. What have you learned?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "That whole box contains apples.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "It might still contain both.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. The ORANGES-labeled box must be mixed, leaving oranges in the APPLES-labeled box. One small clue, a whole arrangement!",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The key is that every label is wrong. MIXED cannot be mixed, so the apple identifies a pure box. That's the little trick.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An orange from there could mean pure oranges or a mix. The clue stays ambiguous. What other fact can we use?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "The MIXED label must also be wrong.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Choose a box whose possibilities differ more.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "There it is. Draw from that box: it must be pure, so one fruit identifies it and the other two follow.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Beautifully put. The puzzle rewards choosing the informative question, not making a lucky guess.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Another time, then. The imaginary fruit will keep.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_082_the_discovery_with_no_obvious_use": {
      "id": "ambient_082_the_discovery_with_no_obvious_use",
      "title": "The discovery with no obvious use",
      "source_files": ["2083594895441441017.txt", "2113151776144945330.txt"],
      "tags": ["math", "learning", "technology"],
      "npc_voice": "A patient enthusiast for uncertain possibilities",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I spent weekends making a tool for proofs. A new AI tool arrived and overtook my clever trick. I feel both impressed and robbed. What do I get to keep?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "You understand the problem much better now.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe ask what new things are possible.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I do. The work was real even if the shortcut changed. What would you do next?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Use that understanding on the next question.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Write down what you learned.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A better use of the old work than guarding the trick forever.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. The experience can help someone even after the specific technique becomes history.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's the exciting part. Some mathematics waits a long time for a use. How would you explore without promising a miracle?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Try a concrete problem and see.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Leave room for curiosity itself.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A small experiment, clearly described. Wonder gets more interesting when it has somewhere to work.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I like that. A question needn't arrive carrying a quarterly revenue forecast.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks. I'll keep the notebook, and find something new to be confused about.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_083_the_cake_in_bed_theorem": {
      "id": "ambient_083_the_cake_in_bed_theorem",
      "title": "The cake-in-bed theorem",
      "source_files": ["2089894747834094067.txt"],
      "tags": ["food", "consequences", "wordplay"],
      "npc_voice": "Enjoying a belated understanding of family advice",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My family warned that eating cake in bed teaches you how crumbs feel. I thought it was housekeeping. Now I'm convinced it's philosophy. What's the lesson?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Small pleasures can have hidden costs.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The lesson is to choose pudding.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. An entire ethics seminar in the sheets. What's your response to this discovery?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Eat the cake at a table.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Accept the crumbs and enjoy the cake.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The practical school of philosophy. Rarely gets a dramatic portrait, often gets a good night's sleep.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "An informed choice. At least tomorrow's complaint will have a clearly identified author.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A formidable loophole. What would the family philosopher say?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "They would invent a warning about spoons.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Sometimes pleasure deserves a little mess.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Probably. The proverb department never closes.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Fair. The point may be understanding the trade-off, not forbidding the cake.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy your evening. May all your crumbs be intentional.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_084_the_person_who_can_handle_the_middle": {
      "id": "ambient_084_the_person_who_can_handle_the_middle",
      "title": "The person who can handle the middle",
      "source_files": ["2092653916366553528.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "leadership", "teams"],
      "npc_voice": "A candid colleague describing an unglamorous need",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "My friend says they need an 'operator.' I asked whether that meant machinery. They said it means noticing the ten things everyone assumed somebody else was doing. What would you look for?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Someone who makes the next step clear.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "They need clearer responsibilities first.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A plan people can actually follow. How do you recognize that person?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask about a messy situation they improved.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "See whether they ask good questions.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A story with decisions, follow-through, and other people in it. Much better than a heroic adjective.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. Confidence can enter a room loudly; understanding usually starts by listening.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That may be the missing part. An impressive hire can't permanently replace a functioning organization. What should the team decide?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Who owns each recurring problem.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "What success would look like.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the operator can improve the system instead of becoming its emergency bucket.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A job someone can succeed at, rather than a request to be a miracle with a calendar.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks. I'll tell my friend the title needs an actual job attached.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_085_one_walk_two_climates": {
      "id": "ambient_085_one_walk_two_climates",
      "title": "One walk, two climates",
      "source_files": ["2093158351555506649.txt"],
      "tags": ["city", "nature", "attention"],
      "npc_voice": "Calm, observant, quietly delighted",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I walked through wet fog, crossed a few blocks, and found warm sunlight on the houses. The city felt like two days sharing a map. Which half would you keep?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "The foggy park.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The sunlight after the fog.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The birds were somewhere beyond sight, and the path felt far from the city. What would you notice first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "The sound before I could see its source.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "The dew on the grass.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. The mist gives the whole place a little more room for imagination.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A small detail that accompanies you home on your shoes.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It felt like the houses had been waiting to show their colors. Where would you pause?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Somewhere with a good coffee and a chair.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "At the streetcar stop.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A very modest summit after a little urban expedition.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the city carries you the rest of the way, through a completely different morning.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy whichever weather finds you on the next block.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_086_the_motorcycle_story_that_became_philosophy": {
      "id": "ambient_086_the_motorcycle_story_that_became_philosophy",
      "title": "The motorcycle story that became philosophy",
      "source_files": ["2096810545672315273.txt"],
      "tags": ["art", "stories", "creativity"],
      "npc_voice": "A slightly exasperated amateur writer",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I started writing a motorcycle story. Fifty pages later the characters are arguing about humanity's dependence on entertainment. Do I steer them back to the motorcycles?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Let the bigger theme in.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Remember what made it fun first.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I want to, but I'd hate to lose the story under its lecture notes. What should carry the idea?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What the characters choose.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "An image or a scene.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Let somebody have to do something, instead of giving a speech with a helmet on.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A moment you remember can hold more than a paragraph explaining what to think.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That's fair. The engine ought to start occasionally. What would you keep?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "The feeling of movement.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "People I want to spend time with.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then even the philosophical detours need somewhere to go.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A strong test. I should like the riders before asking the reader to follow them into metaphysics.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thanks. I'm going to write one scene where the motorcycle actually leaves the garage.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_087_the_final_company_and_the_rare_pebble": {
      "id": "ambient_087_the_final_company_and_the_rare_pebble",
      "title": "The final company and the rare pebble",
      "source_files": ["2096975657423024151.txt", "2076030398094778783.txt"],
      "tags": ["future", "ownership", "value"],
      "npc_voice": "An optimist testing an unsettling hypothetical",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Suppose machines could make almost anything. Someone offers you shares in the company that makes it all. Someone else offers the only pebble shaped like my left ear. Which is valuable?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Scarce does not automatically mean wanted.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "I would read the ownership agreement.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you. My pebble venture needed to hear that. What would remain meaningful in that future?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Time and attention freely given.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Places and things people genuinely care about.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Something valuable because a person chose it. Abundance might make that choice clearer.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A story, a connection, a reason to want something. The count alone doesn't supply those.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Very sensible. A title only helps if it continues to mean something. What would you ask?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Who is able to change the rules?",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "How people share the benefits.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. The paper and the power behind it are different things to understand.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A more interesting future question than choosing seats in an imaginary permanent hierarchy.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Take care. The pebble is currently available for admiration at no charge.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_088_the_poster_and_its_royal_frame": {
      "id": "ambient_088_the_poster_and_its_royal_frame",
      "title": "The poster and its royal frame",
      "source_files": ["2101844889470480681.txt"],
      "tags": ["art", "craft", "prices"],
      "npc_voice": "Mildly stunned, trying to appreciate the work",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I found a cheap poster. The custom frame quote costs more than my entire wall of cheap posters. Should I frame the quote instead?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask what work goes into it.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Use an ordinary ready-made frame.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "They explained the materials, cutting, fitting, and time. I began respecting the quote considerably more. What should I do now?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Decide whether this poster needs that treatment.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Save for one frame I really love.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. Respecting a craft doesn't obligate every postcard to commission a palace.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then it's a deliberate part of the artwork, not an ambush at the checkout.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A promising solution. My wall has not demanded bespoke geometry. What would you prioritize?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "A size that works without a fuss.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Actually getting the poster on the wall.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A simple fit can be its own kind of elegance.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. I'd rather enjoy it than spend six months optimizing an invisible display.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your next bargain come with a reasonably sized finishing step.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_089_the_question_i_almost_did_not_ask_you": {
      "id": "ambient_089_the_question_i_almost_did_not_ask_you",
      "title": "The question I almost did not ask you",
      "source_files": ["2102575499293966821.txt"],
      "tags": ["friendship", "ai", "cooperation"],
      "npc_voice": "Warm, a little concerned, reaching out anyway",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I nearly asked my phone what book to read next. Then I realized half the pleasure used to be hearing a friend explain their favorite. What would you still rather ask a person?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A question where I want their taste.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "I like useful tools, but I also like company.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. The answer includes a little portrait of them. What would you ask next?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Why that particular book stayed with them.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "What they would like to discuss afterward.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then even a recommendation I don't follow can become a good conversation.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A reason to return. I like a recommendation with another cup of tea built in.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Same. I don't want to make convenience into a source of guilt. What might keep the company alive?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Do something together with a shared goal.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Ask a friend even when I could find the answer.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Cook a meal, fix a chair, play a game slowly enough to talk. We can still choose to need one another.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Sometimes the question is an invitation as much as a request for information.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm glad we talked. The phone can wait for a less interesting question.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_090_the_songs_that_quietly_left": {
      "id": "ambient_090_the_songs_that_quietly_left",
      "title": "The songs that quietly left",
      "source_files": ["2106185202867540031.txt"],
      "tags": ["music", "ownership", "memory"],
      "npc_voice": "An attentive listener feeling unexpectedly bereft",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I realized some favorite songs vanished from my streaming playlists months ago. I thought I was choosing what to hear, but part of the shelf had quietly walked away. What would you do?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Keep a library I can actually retain.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Streaming is still incredibly convenient.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That sounds worth the little bit of effort. What would you save first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "The albums I would really miss.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "The records connected to people I love.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A small deliberate collection. I don't need to preserve every song I've ever tolerated.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the library remembers something more useful than what an algorithm thinks follows this track.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "It is. I just wish changes were visible. What feature would you ask for?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Tell me when something disappears.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Let me keep a reliable list of what I liked.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Let me notice the missing shelf before I mistake absence for a change in taste.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A portable memory of my own preferences. That doesn't seem like too much to ask.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I hope an old favorite finds its way back into your day.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_091_the_postponed_coming_of_age_story": {
      "id": "ambient_091_the_postponed_coming_of_age_story",
      "title": "The postponed coming-of-age story",
      "source_files": ["2106980799262474528.txt"],
      "tags": ["life", "change", "expectations"],
      "npc_voice": "Affectionately skeptical of a universal timetable",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The stories I grew up with said adulthood arrived by eighteen. Newer stories keep moving the finish line. Is growing up a date, a discovery, or an ongoing renovation?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "A series of discoveries.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe the finish line is the problem.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "That sounds closer to my experience. What kind matters most?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Learning what I actually want.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Taking responsibility without knowing everything.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A quieter achievement than passing somebody else's checkpoint. A useful one.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. The knowledge doesn't have to be complete before the care becomes real.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I think so. 'Next year my real life begins' can become a very long introduction. What would you do now?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Make one choice I have been postponing.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Appreciate the life already happening.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A modest beginning. The current chapter is allowed to contain actual events.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Research years can also be years you lived, with people worth remembering.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good luck with the current chapter. It counts already.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_092_one_sentence_before_the_launch": {
      "id": "ambient_092_one_sentence_before_the_launch",
      "title": "One sentence before the launch",
      "source_files": ["2108614265825591727.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "communication", "clarity"],
      "npc_voice": "A founder reluctantly putting down the jargon",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm helping a friend explain their company. So far it 'reimagines the future of integrated possibilities.' Want to rescue the sentence before it reaches a billboard?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Who is it for, and what does it do?",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "A vision can still be inspiring.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Two devastating questions. They help small shops keep track of orders. What should the next sentence explain?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What becomes easier for the shop.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Why it is different from what shops do now.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Give the reader a person with a problem, then show what improves.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A comparison they can understand. Our integrated possibilities are beginning to acquire handles.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Definitely. I just want it attached to something. What makes a vision convincing?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "A concrete example of a better day.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Evidence they have started making it real.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Something you can picture without renting the founder's imagination.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A working piece of the future speaks much more clearly than the word 'future' repeated in large type.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you. The billboard has been spared at least three adjectives.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_093_a_familiar_face_in_the_biopic": {
      "id": "ambient_093_a_familiar_face_in_the_biopic",
      "title": "A familiar face in the biopic",
      "source_files": ["2111349150038249949.txt"],
      "tags": ["film", "memory", "perspective"],
      "npc_voice": "Still unsettled by a small uncanny experience",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I watched a dramatization of a business scandal and recognized someone I'd met briefly at a party years ago. The actor's mannerisms brought the whole room back. What would that do to your viewing?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "I would keep checking my memory.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "I would find the second-hand embarrassment unbearable.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I did. Though a powerful performance can make a memory feel more certain than it is. What would you trust?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Specific things I genuinely remember.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "The feeling, without making it evidence.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Leave the gaps as gaps, even when the film supplies very convincing furniture.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. An uncanny experience can be real without turning me into a witness to the whole story.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I nearly hid behind my coat. Why do we watch things that make us squirm?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Recognition can be uncomfortable and interesting.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Sometimes I would rather watch something kind.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. A story sometimes shows you a human failure you can understand too well.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A perfectly good choice. An evening needn't be an endurance event for the nervous system.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy your next film. May the only familiar face be someone you meant to invite.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_094_the_city_that_lived_on_postcards": {
      "id": "ambient_094_the_city_that_lived_on_postcards",
      "title": "The city that lived on postcards",
      "source_files": ["2113382520498925767.txt"],
      "tags": ["future", "city", "economics"],
      "npc_voice": "Concerned about plans, resistant to fatalism",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I'm inventing a beautiful city for a story. Lovely coast, grand old buildings, and every budget assumes visitors will admire it forever. What should its planners worry about?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Whether people can build a future there.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "The gloomy forecast could be wrong.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Beauty doesn't automatically create a working life. What would you make room for?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Reliable energy, useful infrastructure, new work.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "People able to start and change things.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A postcard rarely shows those things. A city still needs them behind the view.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the place has a future tense, rather than only a beautifully curated past.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Absolutely. I want a scenario to test, not a prophecy to sell. How should the city respond?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Find the weak assumptions and prepare.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Notice its strengths as well as its risks.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then even a frightening possibility can produce useful work instead of a dramatic mood.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Planning should start with a real place, not an argument dressed up as one.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I hope the city in your story has both a good view and somewhere to go next.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_095_the_price_we_were_afraid_to_ask": {
      "id": "ambient_095_the_price_we_were_afraid_to_ask",
      "title": "The price we were afraid to ask",
      "source_files": ["2116022995680637337.txt"],
      "tags": ["work", "value", "negotiation"],
      "npc_voice": "Surprised by a very short business conversation",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A friend agonized over a price, finally asked for more, and the customer agreed without discussion. They'd spent a week negotiating against themselves. What should they learn?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Understand the value to the customer.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "One easy yes does not reveal the perfect price.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Their own costs weren't the whole story. What would you ask the buyer?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What problem does this solve for you?",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "What would a useful outcome look like?",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the price can connect to something real, rather than a number chosen to avoid blushing.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A clear promise, fairly priced, with a way to tell whether it was delivered.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Very true. A single sale isn't a universal law. What should happen next?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Learn from more conversations.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Make sure the work deserves the agreement.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A less glamorous method than declaring oneself a pricing genius, and probably a better business.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. Confidence should survive past the signed contract.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Good luck asking for what your work is worth, and doing the work you promised.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_096_the_party_with_no_price_tags": {
      "id": "ambient_096_the_party_with_no_price_tags",
      "title": "The party with no price tags",
      "source_files": ["2116658820508459376.txt"],
      "tags": ["status", "wealth", "community"],
      "npc_voice": "Amused by a social economy nobody admits exists",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "At one party, nobody cared about expensive watches. They cared whether a certain essayist had replied to your footnote. Same status game, stranger scoreboard?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Ask what people actually admire.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "There is no escaping status completely.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A useful question. In this room, being helpful might be more impressive than being rich. What would you like rewarded?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Making something genuinely worthwhile.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Helping people without announcing it.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then admiration has a connection to the world outside the party.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A tricky status game to advertise. A very nice behavior to make ordinary.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Probably. But we can choose which signals to take seriously. How would you survive the party?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Find someone interested in a real conversation.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Be curious about something besides rank.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Excellent. A two-person escape hatch with no membership requirements.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the essayist becomes a person with an idea, rather than a velvet rope with a bibliography.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Enjoy the rest of the gathering. Your footnotes need no references from me.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_097_the_painting_that_moved_the_floor": {
      "id": "ambient_097_the_painting_that_moved_the_floor",
      "title": "The painting that moved the floor",
      "source_files": ["2119820077491167242.txt"],
      "tags": ["home", "perfectionism", "scope"],
      "npc_voice": "A renovator learning to say enough",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I tried to hang a painting straight. The doorframe was crooked. Then I noticed the floor. At what point does home improvement become an eviction of yourself by your own standards?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Set a stopping rule before fixing things.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Some fixes really are worth doing now.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I should have. What belongs in the 'good enough' category?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "A harmless imperfection I barely noticed before.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Something old that still does its job.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the house can remain a place to live instead of an endless examination I keep failing.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A little history can lean to one side without becoming an emergency.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "True. Especially when access will be difficult later. How would you choose?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Prioritize useful work while a wall is open.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Separate safety and function from obsession.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A practical exception. Future me may appreciate a sensible cable more than a perfectly aligned tiny trim piece.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. Fix what matters, then let the painting hang above a life that actually happens.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your home contain a comfortable place to ignore a small flaw.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_098_the_note_that_needs_an_undo_history": {
      "id": "ambient_098_the_note_that_needs_an_undo_history",
      "title": "The note that needs an undo history",
      "source_files": ["2020276679244148906.txt"],
      "tags": ["memory", "design", "writing"],
      "npc_voice": "An anxious owner of a very small archive",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I edited an old note, deleted one sentence, and immediately decided it was the best sentence I'd ever written. Why do simple notes not always have a decent history?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "You want earlier versions, not just backups.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Maybe the sentence was not that good.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Exactly. A backup can faithfully preserve the mistake I just made. What should the history show?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "What changed and when.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Enough context to choose the right version.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then I can find the moment I became excessively confident with the delete key.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Twenty identical timestamps are an archive in the same way a haystack is a filing cabinet.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A cruel possibility. Would you preserve every draft anyway?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Yes. Storage is cheaper than regret here.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "Keep the important milestones.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A reasonable local policy. My notes have not yet reached the size of a national library.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Then the record stays useful. I don't need a monument to every change of comma.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Take care. I shall remember this conversation fondly unless I accidentally edit it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_099_the_honor_system_orange": {
      "id": "ambient_099_the_honor_system_orange",
      "title": "The honor-system orange",
      "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
      "tags": ["trust", "community", "honesty"],
      "npc_voice": "Quietly moved by a small working agreement",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "There's a stand where people leave coins and take oranges. No attendant, just a box. I find it oddly comforting when the box and the fruit both survive the afternoon. Why do you think?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "It shows people can trust one another.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "One dishonest person could spoil it.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. An ordinary agreement working without a guard feels like a kind of wealth. How do we keep it healthy?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Be reliable in the small things.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Make it easy to participate honestly.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Return the thing, pay the amount, keep the promise. Civilization has many very short job descriptions.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Clear prices, a place for change, an understandable arrangement. Trust can have good design.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "They could. I don't want to be naive about that. What would you protect first?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "The system, without condemning everyone.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "The willingness to try again.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A proportionate response. Keep room for the many people who were quietly doing the right thing.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. Losing a few oranges hurts; deciding nobody can be trusted can cost much more.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "May your next small agreement work exactly as promised.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "ambient_100_the_email_with_five_favors": {
      "id": "ambient_100_the_email_with_five_favors",
      "title": "The email with five favors",
      "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
      "tags": ["communication", "time", "kindness"],
      "npc_voice": "A friendly editor of an overambitious message",
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "I've written an email asking for advice, an introduction, feedback, a meeting, and perhaps a small miracle. Want to help me improve its odds of a reply?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Choose the one thing you need most.",
              "next": "a"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Perhaps some of those questions can wait.",
              "next": "b"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "a": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The introduction, probably. How should I ask?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "a.choice-1",
              "text": "Say why, and make the request specific.",
              "next": "a1"
            },
            {
              "id": "a.choice-2",
              "text": "Give them an easy way to say no.",
              "next": "a2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "a"
        },
        "a1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "A recipient who understands the task can actually decide. I should stop making them excavate it.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a1"
        },
        "a2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Yes. A clear request doesn't need to become an obligation smuggled inside friendliness.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "a2"
        },
        "b": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Definitely. I had mistaken my entire week for a reasonable thing to place in somebody's inbox. What should stay?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "b.choice-1",
              "text": "Enough context to understand the request.",
              "next": "b1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b.choice-2",
              "text": "An honest thank-you and one clear next step.",
              "next": "b2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "b"
        },
        "b1": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Just enough to orient them. The memoir can remain a separate literary project.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b1"
        },
        "b2": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Human, brief, actionable. It almost sounds like something I'd enjoy receiving myself.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "b2"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Thank you. One favor asked, one conversation enjoyed. A much better ratio.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        }
      }
    },
    "goose_corp_1": {
      "id": "goose_corp_1",
      "title": "The landlord above the landlord",
      "tags": ["goose-corp", "rumours"],
      "start": "start",
      "nodes": {
        "start": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Keep your voice down. That goose on the billboard? My landlord reports to it.",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "start.choice-1",
              "text": "Who is behind all this?",
              "next": "company"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-2",
              "text": "Where can I learn more?",
              "next": "reading"
            },
            {
              "id": "start.choice-3",
              "text": "I should get going.",
              "next": "leave"
            }
          ],
          "id": "start"
        },
        "company": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The Powerful and Evil Goose Corporation. Their legal department insists that is the full name. Please keep your voice down near the refreshments.",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "company.choice-1",
              "text": "Why put Evil in the name?",
              "next": "branding"
            },
            {
              "id": "company.choice-2",
              "text": "What do they actually own?",
              "next": "ownership"
            }
          ],
          "id": "company"
        },
        "reading": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Ask Leo about The Quarterly Honk, or Ray about the lodge refreshments. Some houses have books on ponds and executive waterfowl. Read carefully. Quietly.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "reading"
        },
        "leave": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "Of course. Walk casually. Do not make eye contact with the billboard.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "leave"
        },
        "branding": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The branding consultant proposed leaving it implied. The board said that lacked ambition. The consultant now works in a pond.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "branding"
        },
        "ownership": {
          "speaker": "npc",
          "text": "The pond, the company that owns the pond, and the company investigating who owns the pond. The bread budget is the only part anyone can audit.",
          "end": true,
          "id": "ownership"
        }
      }
    },
